sk': 'Real Estate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/122606bf-96d6-52e7-a530-1d526ac40213', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/122606bf-96d6-52e7-a530-1d526ac40213'}, {'abstract': 'This week’s properties include a townhouse in the Annex area and a condo in Moss Park.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/02/realestate/homes-for-sale-in-toronto.html', 'snippet': 'This week’s properties include a townhouse in the Annex area and a condo in Moss Park.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After several months of declining home prices and sales, Toronto’s real estate market seems to be rebounding. Many brokers say that as inventory has declined, they are seeing bully offers make a comeback. (A bully offer is an offer that is submitted before a designated “offer day” when the seller plans to accept offers.) The rebound has not extended to neighboring provinces though. Last week, the Canadian Real Estate Association announced market activity across the country was down 9.9 percent in August and sales had dropped from the year before in 60 percent of local Canadian markets.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Homes for Sale in Toronto', 'kicker': 'On the Market', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Toronto (Ontario)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Condominiums', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-02T15:20:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Deschamps', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Deschamps', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'ra