': 'City Saucery sells preserved local tomatoes at several Greenmarkets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the local tomato season winds down, the frivolous grasshoppers among us who did not diligently can batches of them for winter dinners have a new resource. Amid the overflowing stands of shiny red orbs still in the markets in early fall are bright jars of preserved local, organic tomatoes sold by Jorge Moret, a partner in City Saucery. The company uses the recipes of Carolina Marino, a native of Calabria, Italy, and is run by her son Michael Marino and his companion, Mr. Moret. The jarred tomatoes include yellow ones and a sauce made from bruised “ugly” tomatoes. The company also sells Calabrian-style sauces and condiments online and in stores: City Saucery summer tomatoes, Union Square, Fort Greene and McCarren Park Greenmarkets; sauces and condiments, $14.98 and up, citysaucery.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/04/dining/04BURNER6/04BURNER6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/04/dining/04BURNER6/04BURNER6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/04/dining/04BURNER6/04BURNER6-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/04/dining/04BURNER6/04BURNER6-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/04/dining/04BURNER6/04BURNER6-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/04/dining/04BURNER6/04BURNER6-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/04/dining/04BURNER6/04BURNER6-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Jarred Tomatoes Capture the Fleeting Flavors of Summer', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Savor: Summer Tomatoes Packed Up in Jars', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tomatoes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'City Saucery', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Union Square Greenmarket', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-02T15:31:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aeb94198-0b8d-5420-bd4f-45d94e81a7c0', 'word_count': 153, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aeb94198-0b8d-5420-bd4f-45d94e81a7c0'}, {'abstract': 'Niman Ranch’s cured ham is aged for at least a year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/02/dining/niman-ranch-prosciutto.html', 'snippet': 'Niman Ranch’s cured ham is aged for at least a year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Increasingly, American producers are selling prosciutto. Niman Ranch is the latest. The hams are cured in the traditional fashion — rubbed only with sea salt and lard, without added nitrites or nitrates — and hung to air-dry in stages for at least a year by a processor in Rhode Island. The fragrant, deep rose result, sold as whole hams with and without bone, or sliced in three-ounce consumer packages, is meaty and slightly saline, with good prosciutto’s typical shadow of sweetness. The label says “uncured” because, according to Agriculture Department rules, products made without sodium nitrite or sodium nitrate must be labeled that way: Niman Ranch Prosciutto, $7.99 for three ounces, $199.95 for boneless ham, $250 for bone-in ham, debragga.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/04/dining/04BURNER5/04BURNER5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/04/dining/04BURNER5/04BURNER5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/04/dining/04BURNER5/04BURNER5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/04/dining/04BURNER5/04BURNER5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/04/dining/04BURNER5/04BURNER5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/04/dining/04BURNER5/04BURNER5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/04/dining/04BURNER5/04BURNER5-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A New American Prosciutto', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Serve: Traditional Prosciutto Made in Rhode Island', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labeling and Labels (Product)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Meat', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Niman Ranch', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-02T15:37:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/67c7b2d2-484c-52ae-9109-5c4b8a7c6919', 'word_count': 143, 'uri': 'nyt://article/67c7b2d2-484c-52ae-9109-5c4b8a7c6919'}, {'abstract': 'The shop in the Lotte New York Palace hotel sells pastries and food to go, including apple cider doughnuts and a new take on the black-and-white cookie.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/02/dining/pomme-palais-reopens-in-midtown.html', 'snippet': 'The shop in the Lotte New York Palace hotel sells pastries and food to go, including apple cider doughnuts and a new take on the black-and-white cookie.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pomme Palais has reopened after having been closed all summer. The chef Michel Richard, who died last year, originally opened the shop for pastries and takeout in the New York Palace hotel. Homemade apple cider and cinnamon doughnuts, autumn ginger snaps, pastrami salmon sandwiches and a new take on the black-and-white cookie with an amaretto base highlight the new fall menu: Pomme Palais, Lotte New York Palace, 30 East 51st Street (Madison Avenue), 212-303-7755, pommepalais.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/04/dining/04BURNER1/04BURNER1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 407, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/04/dining/04BURNER1/04BURNER1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 407}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/04/dining/04BURNER1/04BURNER1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 694, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/04/dining/04BURNER1/04BURNER1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 984, 'width': 1451, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/04/dining/04BURNER1/04BURNER1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/04/dining/04BURNER1/04BURNER1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/04/dining/04BURNER1/04BURNER1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pomme Palais Reopens in Midtown', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Indulge: Pomme Palais  Reopens in Midtown', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pomme Palais (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Madison Avenue (Manhattan, NY)