asoline', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric and Hybrid Vehicles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ford Motor Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barra, Mary T', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-02T16:00:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Vlasic and Neal E. Boudette', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vlasic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Neal', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Boudette', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/341a07b9-d90d-5640-83e2-8216a947b50b', 'word_count': 1213, 'uri': 'nyt://article/341a07b9-d90d-5640-83e2-8216a947b50b'}, {'abstract': 'A demonstration next month at the De Gustibus Cooking School will focus on Boston and pasta, among other things.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/02/dining/de-gustibus-barbara-lynch-mark-ladner.html', 'snippet': 'A demonstration next month at the De Gustibus Cooking School will focus on Boston and pasta, among other things.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pasta will be just one subject of a conversation at the De Gustibus Cooking School on Nov. 20 between Barbara Lynch, the Boston chef and restaurateur, and Mark Ladner, the former Del Posto chef whose soon-to-open Pasta Flyer will put a new spin on fast-service spaghetti. Expect them to demonstrate some pasta-making tips and recipes, and along the way, perhaps divulge some revelations. (Ms. Lynch is the author of the tell-all memoir “Out of Line,” and Mr. Ladner, who worked in Boston, can share memories with her.) Food and wine will be served: 6 to 8:30 p.m., Nov. 20, $115, De Gustibus Cooking School, Macy’s Herald Square, 151 West 34th Street, 212-239-1652, degustibusnyc.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/04/dining/04Burner8/04Burner8-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/04/dining/04Burner8/04Burner8-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/04/dining/04Burner8/04Burner8-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/04/dining/04Burner8/04Burner8-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 502, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/04/dining/04Burner8/04Burner8-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 502}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/04/dining/04Burner8/04Burner8-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 857, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/04/dining/04Burner8/04Burner8-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1675, 'width': 2002, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Evening With the Chefs Barbara Lynch and Mark Ladner', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Learn: Chefs to Share Views On Pasta, and More', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pasta', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ladner, Mark', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lynch, Barbara', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-02T16:01:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4fff6ded-9971-5b0e-9556-a96281931127', 'word_count': 136, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4fff6ded-9971-5b0e-9556-a96281931127'}, {'abstract': 'The museum celebrates the 50th anniversary of Tanaquil Le Clercq’s ‘Ballet Cook Book’ with two nights of discussion.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/02/dining/ballet-cook-book-tanaquil-le-clercq-guggenheim.html', 'snippet': 'The museum celebrates the 50th anniversary of Tanaquil Le Clercq’s ‘Ballet Cook Book’ with two nights of discussion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The ballerina Tanaquil Le Clercq, a star of the New York City Ballet and a wife of George Balanchine, was an accomplished cook. Polio ended her dancing career in 1956, so she spent more time in the kitchen and eventually wrote “The Ballet Cook Book” (Stein and Day) with recipes and anecdotes from the files of leading figures in the world of dance at that time. The more than 90 contributors include Alicia Alonso, Erik Bruhn, Leslie Caron, Margot Fonteyn, Serge Lifar, Arthur Mitchell and Edward Villella. It’s an international cookbook with a strong Russian influence and photographs of dancers, not food. Ballet buffs would love it, but for now, it’s out of print. Next month, for the book’s 50th anniversary, there will be a program about it at the Guggenheim Museum, with the dancers Jacques d’Amboise, Allegra Kent, Jared Angle and Adrian Danchig-Waring in a conversation with Meryl Rosofsky, a food scholar. Some dishes from the book will also be served on a special menu (not included in the program price) at the museum’s restaurant, the Wright: Nov. 5 and 6, 7:30 p.m., $40 ($35 for museum members), worksandprocess.org; the Wright, 212-427-5690, opentable.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/04/dining/04BURNER3/04BURNER3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 924, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/04/dining/04BURNER3/04BURNER3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 924}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/04/dining/04BURNER3/04BURNER3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 665, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/04/dining/04BURNER3/04BURNER3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1246, 'width': 809, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/04/dining/04BURNER3/04BURNER3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/04/dining/04BURNER3/04BURNER3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/04/dining/04BURNER3/04BURNER3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Guggenheim Talk Focuses on Legendary Dancer’s Cookbook', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Appreciate: Recipes and Tales From Dancing Fame', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Le Clercq, Tanaquil', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Ballet Cook Book (Book)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Guggenheim, Solomon R, Museum', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-02T16:07:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a88bcfd2-3e66-56a4-b2c8-5d2efa429128', 'word_count': 217, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a88bcfd2-3e66-56a4-b2c8-5d2efa429128'}, {'abstract': 'The new dining room at the Museum of Contemporary Art pays homage to the Venezuelan-American sculptor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/02/dining/marisol-chicago-restaurant.html', 'snippet': 'The new dining room at the Museum of Contemporary Art pays homage to the Venezuelan-American sculptor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To honor the Venezuelan-American artist María Sol Escobar, known as Marisol, who died last year, the Museum of Contemporary Art Chicago has named its new restaurant after her. Decorating the Marisol dining room was the job of the English artist Chris Ofili, who also painted the colorful mural and the other artwork on the walls. The chef Jason Hammel, who owns Lula Cafe in Chicago, features dinner and counter service, and soon, lunch and brunch with menus that are contemporary and long on vegetables. There’s a steak sandwich with egg called At the Spring Street Diner c. 1972, in homage to Marisol, who donated the museum’s first acquisition. She is said to have liked to eat steak and eggs late at night in SoHo in New York: Marisol, 205 East Pearson Street (North Mies van der Rohe Way), Chicago, 312-799-3599, marisolchicago.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/04/dining/04BURNER4/04BURNER4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 402, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/04/dining/04BURNER4/04BURNER4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 402}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/04/dining/04BURNER4/04BURNER4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 687, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/04/dining/04BURNER4/04BURNER4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1373, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/04/dining/04BURNER4/04BURNER4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/04/dining/04BURNER4/04BURNER4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/04/dining/04BURNER4/04BURNER4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Chicago Art Museum Opens a Restaurant Named for M