k': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/d6a041d2-d710-51ce-ba13-ddad22bfd668', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/d6a041d2-d710-51ce-ba13-ddad22bfd668'}, {'abstract': 'The director discusses a sequence featuring Ryan Gosling.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/02/movies/denis-villeneuve-interview-blade-runner-2049.html', 'snippet': 'The director discusses a sequence featuring Ryan Gosling.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Blade Runner 2049” continues a story begun on the big screen 35 years ago. This scene is a simple one, with the detective K, played by Ryan Gosling, wandering through an abandoned city. But the director Denis Villeneuve makes it feel ominous. In the video, Mr. Villeneuve discussed his direction for Mr. Gosling (“Walk slower”) and in and interview, explained the significance of music used in the sequence. Here are excerpts from the conversation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Denis Villeneuve Narrates a Scene From ‘Blade Runner 2049’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Blade Runner 2049 (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Villeneuve, Denis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-02T19:23:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mekado Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mekado', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/88dccda0-48e4-59ee-82bf-3241136de0ac', 'word_count': 334, 'uri': 'nyt://article/88dccda0-48e4-59ee-82bf-3241136de0ac'}, {'abstract': 'The director Denis Villeneuve tries to both honor Ridley Scott’s 1982 dystopian classic and to slip free of its considerable shadow.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/02/movies/blade-runner-2049-review-ryan-gosling-harrison-ford.html', 'snippet': 'The director Denis Villeneuve tries to both honor Ridley Scott’s 1982 dystopian classic and to slip free of its considerable shadow.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A lot of the movies released in the late 1970s and early ’80s have spawned franchises, merchandising empires and what we are now invited to call “cinematic universes.” “Blade Runner,” Ridley Scott’s initially underrated 1982 adaptation of a novel by Philip K. Dick, accomplished something more unusual. It sent tendrils of influence — pictorial, conceptual and spiritual — into every corner of the culture and inspired a mystery cult.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/06/arts/06bladerunner1/06bladerunner1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/06/arts/06bladerunner1/06bladerunner1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/06/arts/06bladerunner1/06bladerunner1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/06/arts/06bladerunner1/06bladerunner1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/06/arts/06bladerunner1/06bladerunner1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'imag