ay-revival-race.html', 'snippet': 'Denzel Washington and other cast members reflect on the legacy of the Pulitzer Prize-winning “A Soldier’s Play,” which is being revived Off Broadway.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Charles Fuller’s drama “A Soldier’s Play” had its world premiere Off Broadway in 1981, the playwright envisioned an audience — and a public — that was ready to face uncomfortable truths about the enduring, unwieldy legacy of white supremacy in America. It had been nearly two decades since the passage of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, and Mr. Fuller had grown weary of what he called “the simple racial conflict,” in which white characters and black ones are neatly arrayed on opposite sides of a battlefield.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/02/arts/02SOLDIER-COMBO/02SOLDIER-COMBO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/02/arts/02SOLDIER-COMBO/02SOLDIER-COMBO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/02/arts/02SOLDIER-COMBO/02SOLDIER-COMBO-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/02/arts/02SOLDIER-COMBO/02SOLDIER-COMBO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/02/arts/02SOLDIER-COMBO/02SOLDIER-COMBO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/02/arts/02SOLDIER-COMBO/02SOLDIER-COMBO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/02/arts/02SOLDIER-COMBO/02SOLDIER-COMBO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Play About Racism’s Aftershocks Returns With New Resonance', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Drama on Racial Identity Resonates Anew', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': "A Soldier's Play (Play)", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fuller, Charles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Negro Ensemble Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Washington, Denzel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Theater 80', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weldon, Charles', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pickens, James Jr', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Friedman, Peter (1949- )', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Washington, Adrain', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tucker, Gil', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Glasper, Horace', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-03T19:48:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Reggie Ugwu', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Reggie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ugwu', 'qualifier': None, 'title': 