/arts/fyre-festival-organizer-pleads-not-guilty-to-fraud-charges.html', 'snippet': 'Billy McFarland, whose would-be luxury festival crashed and burned in the Bahamas, faces a maximum penalty of 20 years if he is convicted of defrauding investors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Billy McFarland, the entrepreneur who became a lightning rod in April after his ambitiously marketed Fyre Festival devolved from a would-be luxury getaway into a jamboree of schadenfreude and cold cheese sandwiches, pleaded not guilty to charges of fraud in United States District Court in Manhattan on Monday. Mr. McFarland, 25, who was arrested and charged in June, is accused of misrepresenting financial information about his company to investors who paid him $1.2 million.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/30/arts/30fyrefest1/30fyrefest1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/30/arts/30fyrefest1/30fyrefest1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/30/arts/30fyrefest1/30fyrefest1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/30/arts/30fyrefest1/30fyrefest1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 497, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/30/arts/30fyrefest1/30fyrefest1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 497}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/30/arts/30fyrefest1/30fyrefest1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 7