.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I think people are going to have to take steps in their own lives to take precautions. To protect themselves. And in situations like that, you know, try to stay safe. As somebody said — get small.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day: Conversation Turns to Guns, Then Republicans Change the Subject', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quote of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2017-10-04T00:03:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Today’s Paper', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eab5cf5f-29c1-565a-a5bc-19565b8807ef', 'word_count': 58, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eab5cf5f-29c1-565a-a5bc-19565b8807ef'}, {'abstract': 'If background checks can’t stop this, we need something else.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/03/opinion/vegas-shooting-gun-control-paddock.html', 'snippet': 'If background checks can’t stop this, we need something else.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We live in a country where so long as you follow the rules, you have relatively unfettered access to weapons capable of mass devastation. This week, we can see once again the carnage the rules have made possible. The number of victims of the terrorism in Las Vegas this week is staggering — at least 59 dead and more than 500 injured.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/04/opinion/04gaySub/04gaySub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/04/opinion/04gaySub/04gaySub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None,