anization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/46f32563-e2e0-5f7e-8578-39fa22ebe611', 'word_count': 892, 'uri': 'nyt://article/46f32563-e2e0-5f7e-8578-39fa22ebe611'}, {'abstract': 'Pressed by lawmakers, Defense Secretary Jim Mattis reiterated his view that the Iran accord is working, a quiet break with President Trump.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/03/world/middleeast/mattis-iran-deal-trump.html', 'snippet': 'Pressed by lawmakers, Defense Secretary Jim Mattis reiterated his view that the Iran accord is working, a quiet break with President Trump.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Days before President Trump has to make a critical decision on whether to hold up the Iran nuclear deal, Defense Secretary Jim Mattis openly split with him on abandoning the agreement, the second senior member of the president’s national security team to recently contradict him.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/04/us/-04dc-military1/-04dc-military1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/04/us/-04dc-military1/-04dc-military1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/04/us/-04dc-military1/-04dc-military1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/04/us/-04dc-military1/-04dc-military1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/04/us/-04dc-military1/-04dc-military1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth'