 a forest in the park, thousands of shrubs and trees are being planted.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A black goat named Eyebrows and his sand-colored pals, Lily Belle and Swiss Cheese, lay sunbathing atop their wooden lean-to at the highest point of Prospect Park. Their job was done, their time in Brooklyn coming to an end.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/08/nyregion/08wip/08wip-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/08/nyregion/08wip/08wip-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/08/nyregion/08wip/08wip-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/08/nyregion/08wip/08wip-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/08/nyregion/08wip/08wip-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/08/nyregion/08wip/08wip-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/08/nyregion/08wip/08wip-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Prospect Park, First the Goats, Then the Shrubbery', 'kicker': 'Works in Progress', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Prospect Park, Gardeners With Hooves', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Prospect Park (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Trees and Shrubs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Invasive Species', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Goats', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Flowers and Plants', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Prospect Park Alliance', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-05T11:00:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metropolitan', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Helene Stapinski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Helene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stapinski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/674666d7-a8f6-51fa-9a58-b8d073c07384', 'word_count': 920, 'uri': 'nyt://article/674666d7-a8f6-51fa-9a58-b8d073c07384'}, {'abstract': 'Rooney Mara and Ben Mendelsohn deliver unflinching performances in “Una,” an adaptation of David Harrower’s provocative play “Blackbird.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/05/movies/una-review-rooney-mara.html', 'snippet': 'Rooney Mara and Ben Mendelsohn deliver unflinching performances in “Una,” an adaptation of David Harrower’s provocative play “Blackbird.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'This movie begins with a shot of a girl in her early teens, sitting outside a house, then going into the yard next door, turning a corner, and seeing … something. In a matching cut, Rooney Mara, playing the same character years later, stands in a dark room with strangers as strobe lights flash and a synthetic percussion track throbs. Regardless of what the director, Benedict Andrews, intends, the aggregate effect is “Something bad happened to this person and now she’s into EDM.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/06/movies/06UNA1/merlin-to-scoop-128079461-129079-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/06/movies/06UNA1/merlin-to-scoop-128079461-129079-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/06/movies/06UNA1/merlin-to-scoop-128079461-129079-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/06/movies/06UNA1/merlin-to-scoop-128079461-129079-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 334, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/06/movies/06UNA1/merlin-to-scoop-128079461-129079-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 334}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/06/movies/06UNA1/merlin-to-scoop-128079461-129079-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 569, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/06/movies/06UNA1/merlin-to-scoop-128079461-129079-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1138, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘Una’ Examines an Abuser and His Victim', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Una', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'val