ffer opportunities to spy the birds: On Saturday, a guide will lead a garden walk at noon, while on Sunday the educator Gabriel Willow will conduct both a fall birding walk at 9:30 a.m. and a nature walk at noon that will investigate the site’s furry and finned creatures, too. But the signature event is on Monday at 1 p.m., when Brian Bradley, a master falconer with Skyhunters in Flight, will present the weekend’s stars: species like a gyrfalcon (above, with Mr. Bradley), a great horned owl and a Eurasian eagle owl, which will show off their flight patterns by thrillingly swooping over spectators’ heads. LAUREL GRAEBER', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/06/arts/06listingskids/06listingskids-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/06/arts/06listingskids/06listingskids-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/06/arts/06listingskids/06listingskids-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/06/arts/06listingskids/06listingskids-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 425, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/06/arts/06listingskids/06listingskids-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 425}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/06/arts/06listingskids/06listingskids-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 725, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': N