8ec905-10aa-5abc-8bff-6d494c451300', 'word_count': 1199, 'uri': 'nyt://article/048ec905-10aa-5abc-8bff-6d494c451300'}, {'abstract': 'A landlord wants to inspect apartments in a rent-regulated complex, making tenants anxious.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/07/realestate/do-i-have-to-allow-a-private-investigator-into-my-apartment.html', 'snippet': 'A landlord wants to inspect apartments in a rent-regulated complex, making tenants anxious.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q. I live a in a rent-regulated apartment complex in Corona, Queens. The landlord hired a private investigator to inspect every apartment to “ensure the level of quality in the building.” The inspection company, run by retired police officers, specializes in criminal investigations and surveillance, and uses policing techniques. Tenants must provide photo identification and sign an inspection checklist. This feels like an invasion of privacy that goes beyond typical maintenance-related inspections. Must I comply? If I refuse, could the landlord evict me? ', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/08/realestate/08ASK/08ASK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/08/realestate/08ASK/08ASK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/08/realestate/08ASK/08ASK-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/08/realestate/08ASK/08ASK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 114, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': '