es J. Sykes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Sykes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/c291a9fc-7015-5622-8ff3-645b51468f0b', 'word_count': 1171, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c291a9fc-7015-5622-8ff3-645b51468f0b'}, {'abstract': 'Harvey Weinstein and the predations of progressive men.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/07/opinion/sunday/harvey-weinstein-harassment-liberals.html', 'snippet': 'Harvey Weinstein and the predations of progressive men.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you are surprised by the news that Harvey Weinstein of Miramax fame, a man well known for profane tirades and physical altercations and scrounging M&Ms off movie theater floors, is also the sort of charmer who loafs around semi-nude while asking subordinates for “back” massages, then you can be surprised by just about anything: the sun rising in the east, the fact that movie stars employ plastic surgeons, the news that “The Artist” didn’t actually deserve to win Best Picture.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/08/opinion/sunday/08douthat/08douthat-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 397, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/08/opinion/sunday/08douthat/08douthat-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 397}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/08/opinion/sunday/08douthat/08douthat-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 678, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/08/opinion/sunday/08douthat/08douthat-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1357, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/08/opinion/sunday/08douthat/08douthat-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/08/opinion/sunday/08douthat/08douthat-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/08/opinion/sunday/08douthat/08douthat-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Pigs of Liberalism', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Pigs of Liberalism', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sexual Harassment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weinstein, Harvey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conservatism (US Politics)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Liberalism (US Politics)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-07T18:30:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/d8aab1e1-e8c5-59a8-8386-19feee87b503', 'word_count': 860, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d8aab1e1-e8c5-59a8-8386-19feee87b503'}, {'abstract': 'Hunters like me can help lead the gun control debate away from polemic.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/07/opinion/sunday/responsible-gun-ownership.html', 'snippet': 'Hunters like me can help lead the gun control debate away from polemic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEND, Ore. — When we hike together, my oldest son, who is 5, scans the ground for the perfect “gun.” His ideal stick has an ergonomic crook in it and is a comfortable size to hold. When he finds one like that, he lifts it for a test fire — pew, pew. A mile in, he’s usually got one in each hand but is still on the lookout for an upgrade: anything smoother or more gunlike. My youngest, who is 2, isn’t far behind. He’s been saying the word “gun” for more than a year.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/08/opinion/sunday/08mccaulou/08mccaulou-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 475, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/08/opinion/sunday/08mccaulou/08mccaulou-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 475}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/08/opinion/sunday/08mccaulou/08mccaulou-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 811, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/08/opinion/sunday/08mccaulou/08mccaulou-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1623, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/08/opinion/sunday/08mccaulou/08mccaulou-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/08/opinion/sunday/08mccaulou/08mccaulou-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/08/opinion/sunday/08mccaulou/08mccaulou-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Confessions of a Sensible Gun Owner', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Confessions of a Sensible Gun Owner', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Firearms', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hunting and Trapping', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-07T18:30:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lily Raff Mccaulou', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lily', 'middlename': 'Raff', 'lastname': 'Mccaulou', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/e074dccc-475d-5972-a29b-57c88d3ce176', 'word_count': 1342, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e074dccc-475d-5972-a29b-57c88d3ce176'}, {'abstract': 'My Republican friends think I’m missing something. Am I?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/07/opinion/sunday/trump-republicans-confirmation-bias.html', 'snippet': 'My Republican friends think I’m missing something. Am I?', 'lead_paragraph': 'IT’S an odd feeling when you find yourself effectively living on an island unconnected to people with whom you were once politically close. But it’s a feeling with which I’ve become very familiar.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/08/opinion/sunday/08wehner/08wehner-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 507, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': '