 Is Filling a Void in Late-Night Talk', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Filling a Void  In Late-Night Talk', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BET (TV Network)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thede, Robin', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Rundown With Robin Thede (Program)||Program', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-08T14:00:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a69d2ce6-0a9e-544f-b7a4-2ee482bd0174', 'word_count': 1274, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a69d2ce6-0a9e-544f-b7a4-2ee482bd0174'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Bush Lauren, who lives in the West Village, spends a lot of time on the playground with her toddler, and likes to brunch locally.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/08/nyregion/how-lauren-bush-of-feed-spends-her-sundays.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Bush Lauren, who lives in the West Village, spends a lot of time on the playground with her toddler, and likes to brunch locally.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This year, Lauren Bush Lauren’s company Feed, which has provided 100 million meals to children in need around the world by allocating some of the proceeds from its handbag and jewelry sales to the cause, is celebrating its 10th anniversary. In May, the social business opened its first brick-and-mortar store, the Feed Shop & Cafe, in Dumbo, Brooklyn. Ms. Bush Lauren, 33, who is closely related to two former presidents, lives in the West Village with her husband, David Lauren, 45, who is an executive with Ralph Lauren, and their son, James Lauren, 21 months. SHIVANI VORA', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/08/nyregion/08ROUTINE1/08routine1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/08/nyregion/08ROUTINE1/08routine1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/08/nyregion/08ROUTINE1/08routine1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/08/nyregion/08ROUTINE1/08routine1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/08/nyregion/08ROUTINE1/08routine1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/08/nyregion/08ROUTINE1/08routine1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/08/nyregion/08ROUTINE1/08routine1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Lauren Bush Lauren, C.E.O. of Feed, Spends Her Sundays', 'kicker': 'Sunday Routine', 'cont