uri': 'nyt://article/b369e699-8d08-5185-aba1-57827c7f77e4'}, {'abstract': 'In the violent, male-dominated world of the Times Square sex industry, maybe the question of “Why?” misses the point.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/08/arts/television/the-deuce-what-kind-of-bad-recap.html', 'snippet': 'In the violent, male-dominated world of the Times Square sex industry, maybe the question of “Why?” misses the point.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week’s episode opens with a fake-out. When we hear the command “Order up” over a greasy-spoon breakfast tray, we assume the episode is starting at Leon’s, which serves as a kind of home base for pimps and prostitutes at the beginning of the day. (Or, more likely, the end of the night, given the hours they keep.) But, in fact, we’re in a restaurant in Darlene’s North Carolina hometown, and Darlene is holding court with her old friends, who are calling her by her real name, Donna. The story she’s selling is a powerful one: She’s come back from New York City a more glamorous and confident woman. She’s got a man who’s taking care of her. They, too, can leave their humdrum lives behind and take a bite out of the Big Apple.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/08/watching/08deuce/08deuce-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/08/watching/08deuce/08deuce-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/08/watching/08deuce/08deuce-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/08/watching/08deuce/08deuce-ar