her-columbus-day-statue.html', 'snippet': 'For a generation of immigrants often caricatured as subhuman, Columbus was a figure to rally around against the anti-Italianism of the time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As I watched the disturbing events unfold in Charlottesville, Va., several weeks ago, I knew our Italian-American community would soon be called to once again address questions about statues celebrating Christopher Columbus and the day named in his honor. We would once again be called on to “defend Columbus” against efforts to remake his day into Indigenous People’s Day.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/09/opinion/09violaWeb/09violaWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 384, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/09/opinion/09violaWeb/09violaWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 384}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/09/opinion/09violaWeb/09violaWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 655, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/09/opinion/09violaWeb/09violaWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1178, 'width': 1842, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/09/opinion/09violaWeb/09violaWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/09/opinion/09violaWeb/09violaWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/09/opinion/09violaWeb/09violaWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tearing Down Statues of Columbus Also Tears Down My History', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Monuments and Memorials (Structures)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Columbus Day', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Columbus, Christopher', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Columbus Circle (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-09T07:21:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By John M. Viola', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/17a799e6-f5ea-524a-a0f7-fab6b5914c81', 'word_count': 843, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17a799e6-f5ea-524a-a0f7-fab6b5914c81'}, {'abstract': 'The deluge of stimuli that characterizes our modern life is a hazard: We are being dumped on.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/09/opinion/light-noise-pollution-senses.html', 'snippet': 'The deluge of stimuli that characterizes our modern life is a hazard: We are being dumped on.', 'lead_paragraph': 'People who live in densely populated areas are all too familiar with sensory bombardment — the continuous light and noise pollution that has come to practically define the urban environment. Over time, most city dwellers grow so accustomed to this intense stimulation that they cease to notice it. Their perceptual thresholds, we might say, shift upward.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'm