ns  In Overhaul', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Honeywell International Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shareholder Rights and Activism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Loeb, Daniel S', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Adamczyk, Darius', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-10T13:49:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amie Tsang', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tsang', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c2b65eb-d767-5ef9-b828-81ab629e8ada', 'word_count': 401, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c2b65eb-d767-5ef9-b828-81ab629e8ada'}, {'abstract': 'Sometimes a noble lie, sometimes just a disaster.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2017/10/10/rationality-and-rabbit-holes/', 'snippet': 'Sometimes a noble lie, sometimes just a disaster.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like the vast majority of economists, I was delighted to see Richard Thaler get the Nobel. Anyone with a bit of sense – a group that, believe it or not, includes many economists – knows that people aren’t perfectly rational. But the assumption of hyperrationality still plays far too large a role in the field. And Thaler didn’t just document deviations from rationality, he showed that there are consistent, usable patterns in those deviations.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rationality and Rabbit Holes', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2017-10-10T13:50:50