ss to star: The film producer Harvey Weinstein hired her for the lead in the Jane Austen adaptation “Emma.” Before shooting began, he summoned her to his suite at the Peninsula Beverly Hills hotel for a work meeting that began uneventfully.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/10/us/10actress-alpha/10actress-alpha-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/10/us/10actress-alpha/10actress-alpha-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/10/us/10actress-alpha/10actress-alpha-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1021, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/10/us/10actress-alpha/10actress-alpha-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1021, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/10/us/10actress-alpha/10actress-alpha-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/10/us/10actress-alpha/10actress-alpha-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/10/us/10actress-alpha/10actress-alpha-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Gwyneth Paltrow, Angelina Jolie and Others Say Weinstein Harassed Them', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Big-Name Actresses Say They Were Harassed by Weinstein', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weinstein, Harvey', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sexual Harassment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paltrow, Gwyneth', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jolie, Angelina', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roberts, Tomi-Ann', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Arquette, Rosanna', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kendall, Katherine', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Godreche, Judith', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dunning, Dawn', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-10T17:02:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Investigative', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jodi Kantor and Rachel Abrams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jodi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kantor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Abrams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bfb87e8e-14e4-5cef-96b1-ad6966944c78', 'word_count': 2575, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bfb87e8e-14e4-5cef-96b1-ad6966944c78'}, {'abstract': 'Don Angie, from a husband-and-wife team, opens on Greenwich Avenue; a hotel restaurant with the former Le Turtle chef in the kitchen; and other news.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/10/dining/don-angie-nyc-restaurant-openings.html', 'snippet': 'Don Angie, from a husband-and-wife team, opens on Greenwich Avenue; a hotel restaurant with the former Le Turtle chef in the kitchen; and other news.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DON ANGIE Some married couples strive for a home of their own. For the chefs Scott Tacinelli and Angie Rito, who have been cooking together since 2008, most recently at Quality Italian in Midtown Manhattan, their dream was to own a restaurant. They married in Florence, Italy, in 2015, and now they have their restaurant, a fairly intimate yet airy 58-seat space, done in white with rich marble accents. Both chefs are Italian-American, he from New Jersey and she from Cleveland. They’re putting a personal spin on some classics, like dressing garganelli with a “broken meatball” sauce, putting escargots instead of clams in a preparation for oreganata, using prime rib to make a braciola for two, and tossing a Caesar salad with chrysanthemum greens instead of romaine. “We’re definitely on the same page when it comes to food,” Ms. Rito said. Her husband added, “It’s not easy cooking together, but I trust Angie’s palate more than my own.” They’re also specializing in “red” amaro aperitifs, and the house wine, Don Angie Cali Chianti, is a Sangiovese from California and comes in a bottle wrapped in old-fashioned straw: 103 Greenwich Avenue (12th Street), 212-889-8884, donangienyc.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/11/dining/11OFF/11OFF-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/11/dining/11OFF/11OFF-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/11/dining/11OFF/11OFF-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumb