'person': [{'firstname': 'Alix', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Strauss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b7f58c3d-2983-52e9-a76e-557cb4ebe794', 'word_count': 789, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7f58c3d-2983-52e9-a76e-557cb4ebe794'}, {'abstract': 'Despite all the amenities at the three new stations that opened earlier this year, subway newsstands, those underground mainstays, are not among them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/10/nyregion/second-avenue-subways-newsstands-are-shiny-new-and-empty.html', 'snippet': 'Despite all the amenities at the three new stations that opened earlier this year, subway newsstands, those underground mainstays, are not among them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you have to wait — and wait — for the subway, the stations along the Second Avenue line that opened on Manhattan’s Upper East Side in January are among the nicest places to bide your time. They’re well lit. They have digital countdown clocks. They’re clean, at least as far as subway stations go, and they even have embossed Latin phrases, like “Excelsior,” or “E pluribus unum,” displayed above the stairs.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/07/nyregion/00newsstands1/00newsstands1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/07/nyregion/00newsstands1/00newsstands1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/07/nyregion/00newsstands1/00newsstands1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'captio