 to die. Decades later, she got a message from him.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/10/opinion/auschwitz-israel-holocaust.html', 'snippet': 'To save her own life, she left her father to die. Decades later, she got a message from him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My grandmother Lea once told me a story about the woman who lived next door to her in Tel Aviv, of her capture by the Nazis in Belgium and of an unfathomable decision she had to take to save herself. I never forgot it, and am pleased to share it with you in this Op-Doc film.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'I Have a Message for You', 'kicker': 'Op-Docs', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holocaust and the Nazi Era', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Auschwitz Concentration Camp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tel Aviv (Israel)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Belgium', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-10T19:09:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matan Rochlitz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rochlitz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/371140ff-e99e-5f04-896a-623b95a2bcef', 'word_count': 467, 'uri': 'nyt://article/371140ff-e99e-5f04-896a-623b95a2bcef'}, {'abstract': 'The Swiss-based Martin Ennals Foundation gives its annual prize to Mohamed Zaree of the Cairo Institut