iginal': 'Interview by Ana Marie Cox', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Interview', 'middlename': 'Ana', 'lastname': 'Marie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b6e053f7-6f7b-522f-aee2-6618e3928f06', 'word_count': 702, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6e053f7-6f7b-522f-aee2-6618e3928f06'}, {'abstract': 'Kittie Weston-Knauer, also known as Miss Kittie, has raced against men and keeps cycling despite knee and hip replacements. She explains how BMX is keeping her young in mind and body.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/us/100000005451144/oldest-female-bmx-racer-kittie-weston-knauer.html', 'snippet': 'Kittie Weston-Knauer, also known as Miss Kittie, has raced against men and keeps cycling despite knee and hip replacements. She explains how BMX is keeping her young in mind and body.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kittie Weston-Knauer, also known as Miss Kittie, has raced against men and keeps cycling despite knee and hip replacements. She explains how BMX is keeping her young in mind and body.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/12/us/360-bmx-still/360-bmx-still-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 425, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/12/us/360-bmx-still/360-bmx-still-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 425}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/12/us/360-bmx-still/360-bmx-still-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 725, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/12/us/360-bmx-still/360-bmx-still-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1450, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name':