ouse correspondents Maggie Haberman and Peter Baker will talk with Dean Baquet, the executive editor, on Thursday about covering the Trump administration. Watch live at 6:30 p.m. Eastern.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/11/reader-center/trump-white-house-times-talk.html', 'snippet': 'Our White House correspondents Maggie Haberman and Peter Baker will talk with Dean Baquet, the executive editor, on Thursday about covering the Trump administration. Watch live at 6:30 p.m. Eastern.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Early morning tweets. Frantic Friday resignations and firings. And a looming investigation about Russia. All while news outlets are under increased scrutiny and even dismissed as “fake news.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Is It Like to Cover the Trump White House? Submit Your Questions', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baquet, Dean', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-11T09:00:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'Reader Center', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mikayla Bouchard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mikayla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bouchard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b96da129-fbb7-5d96-8c89-9b04df7a444a', 'word_count': 427, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b96da129-fbb7-5d96-8c89-9b04df7a444a'}, {'abstract': 'The cookbook author and television host always has three iPads, workout gear and, of course, food (including her own hard-boiled eggs).', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/11/travel/how-martha-stewart-travels.html', 'snippet': 'The cookbook author and television host always has three iPads, workout gear and, of course, food (including her own hard-boiled eggs).', 'lead_paragraph': 'Martha Stewart keeps famously busy. She co-hosts a television show with the rapper Snoop Dogg, “Martha & Snoop’s Potluck Dinner Party,” now in its second season on VH1. Her latest book, “Martha Stewart’s Slow Cooker,” was published in August, and she launched her own wine company in the spring.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/22/travel/22MARTHA1/22MARTHA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 614, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/22/travel/22MARTHA1/22MARTHA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 614}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/22/travel/22MARTHA1/22MARTHA1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 867, 'width': 847, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/22/travel/22MARTHA1/22MARTHA1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 867, 'width': 847, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/22/travel/22MARTHA1/22MARTHA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/22/travel/22MARTHA1/22MARTHA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/22/travel/22MARTHA1/22MARTHA1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Martha Stewart Can’t Travel Without', 'kicker': 'Carry-On', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hard-boiled Eggs, iPads and More, but Don’t Rush Her.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stewart, Martha', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-11T09:00:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nell McShane Wulfhart', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nell', 'middlename': 'Mcshane', 'lastname': 'Wulfhart', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cfe53bca-96cb-5515-aba8-12e170304f9b', 'word_count': 760, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cfe53bca-96cb-5515-aba8-12e170304f9b'}, {'abstract': 'The magazine’s Ethicist columnist on balancing competing rights to happiness and why motives matter when seeking to punish others for wrongdoing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/11/magazine/can-my-cat-go-out-if-he-bullies-other-cats.html', 'snippet': 'The magazine’s Ethicist columnist on balancing competing rights to happiness and why motives matter when seeking to punish others for wrongdoing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Playing outside is my cat’s greatest joy. During the long Maine winters, he stares wistfully out the window. The moment the snow melts, he’s outside climbing trees and running laps. The whole street knows my cat, Jasper, by name. Children play with him; he follows the mailman door to door; one neighbor even took photos of him, framed them and gave them to me. ', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/15/magazine/15ethicist/15mag-15ethicist-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 974, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/15/magazine/15ethicist/15mag-15ethicist-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 974}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/15/magazine/15ethicist/15mag-15ethicist-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 632, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/15/magazine/15ethicist/15mag-15ethicist-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1983, 'width': 1222, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/15/magazine/15ethicist/15mag-15ethicist-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/15/magazine/15ethicist/15mag-15ethicist-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/15/magazine/15ethicist/15mag-15ethicist-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Can My Cat Go Out if He Bullies Other Cats?', 'kicker': 'The Ethicist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Can My Cat Go Outside If He Bullies Other Cats? ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Animal Abuse, Rights and Welfare', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philosophy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Happiness', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bullies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Workplace Environment', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Personal)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cats', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lying', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-11T09:00:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kwame Anthony Appiah', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kwame', 'middlename': 'Anthony', 'lastname': 'Appiah', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dde6a4dd-5606-5996-91dc-5491eeaebe7c', 'word_count': 1162, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dde6a4dd-5606-5996-91dc-5491eeaebe7c'}, {'abstract': 'Koyasan is one of the premier destinations for Buddhist pilgrims in Japan. As its popularity peaks, can it still be enjoyed by a visitor seeking quietude?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/11/travel/japan-monastery-koyasan.html', 'snippet': 'Koyasan is one of the premier destinations for Buddhist pilgrims in Japan. As its popularity peaks, can it still be enjoyed by a visitor seeking quietude?', 'lead_paragraph': '“Your eyes should be neither open nor closed,” explained the monk at the front of the room. “They should be sort of sleepy — like a Buddha.” It was my first time meditating, and I was anxious about making some sort of conspicuous misstep. I squinted, then tried to relax my eyelids, but inadvertently began to focus on the bright orange cushion of the person in front of me. I closed my eyes with an inward sigh of exasperation at having such a difficult time following instructions. The monk leading the session told us cheerfully that it might help to rest our vision on the tips of our noses.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/22/travel/22japan1/22japan1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 385, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/22/travel/22japan1/22japan1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 385}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/22/travel/22japan1/22japan1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 657, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/22/travel/22japan1/22japan1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1314, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/22/travel/22japan1/22japan1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/22/travel/22japan1/22japan1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/22/travel/22japan1/22japan1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Seeking Solitude in Japan’s Mountain Monasteries', 'kicker': 'Personal Journeys', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Search for Solitude on a Mountain of Monasteries', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Monasteries and Monks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 