rofits have lifted the markets in the face of challenges, a mirror of global optimism.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/11/business/japan-stocks-nikkei.html', 'snippet': 'A six-quarter growth streak, low unemployment and surging profits have lifted the markets in the face of challenges, a mirror of global optimism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOKYO — Japan still faces deep structural problems. Its population is aging and dwindling. China has stepped up its manufacturing game. Corporate stalwarts like Toshiba and Kobe Steel have stumbled.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/12/world/12japanstocks-1/12japanstocks-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 406, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/12/world/12japanstocks-1/12japanstocks-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 406}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/12/world/12japanstocks-1/12japanstocks-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 692, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/12/world/12japanstocks-1/12japanstocks-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1384, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/12/world/12japanstocks-1/12japanstocks-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/12/world/12japanstocks-1/12japanstocks-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/12/world/12japanstocks-1/12japanstocks-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Japan Stocks Hit 21-Year High as Investors Shrug Off Concerns', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nikkei Stock Average', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-11T10:29:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Soble', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Soble', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c9900ba2-e85d-5fd6-a1ed-1ebeac69587c', 'word_count': 664, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c9900ba2-e85d-5fd6-a1ed-1ebeac69587c'}, {'abstract': 'Christopher Robin is more of a marketable commodity than a beloved son in this film by Simon Curtis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/11/movies/goodbye-christopher-robin-review-domhnall-gleeson.html', 'snippet': 'Christopher Robin is more of a marketable commodity than a beloved son in this film by Simon Curtis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As predictable as mermaid frocks at the Oscars, Hollywood greets the end of the year by suddenly noticing that roughly a third of moviegoers (and three-quarters of art-house audiences) are over 50, most of them women. This annual phenomenon can lead to theaters clogged with old-lady bait, which usually means something British and upper-crusty, preferably with literary roots. A dollop of war, a death or two, and it’s off to the awards r