', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/11/opinion/columnists/11leonhardtnewsletter/merlin-to-scoop-128020340-697616-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Here, Breathe This Coal', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pruitt, Scott', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hill, Jemele', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coal', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Air Pollution', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-11T12:22:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Leonhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leonhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/c9a8d8e3-e1ff-5230-b8d0-7c7595e96ada', 'word_count': 374, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c9a8d8e3-e1ff-5230-b8d0-7c7595e96ada'}, {'abstract': 'In an ancient city of stone and caves, what was old is new again.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/11/t-magazine/travel/matera-italy-guide.html', 'snippet': 'In an ancient city of stone and caves, what was old is new again.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One look at Matera, in Italy’s deep south, and you’ll wonder why the historic Puglian towns of Ostuni and Lecce get all the attention. This city of pale gold limestone, just over the border from Puglia in Basilicata, has more layers than a sfogliatella pastry: Its two cave districts, Sasso Barisano and Sasso Caveoso, are composed of individual dwellings carved into fossil-stuffed strata and stacked on top of each other like cells in a haphazardly constructed beehive. They were inhabited from prehistory until the 1950s, when — overcrowded, poverty-stricken and disease-ridden — they were evacuated by the state. Dubbed “the shame of Italy,” Matera remained largely abandoned for decades. In the 1990s, the Sassi became playgrounds for Matera’s errant youth.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '128', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/11/t-magazine/11tmag-matera-slide-VHKF-copy/11tmag-matera-slide-VHKF-copy-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/11/t-magazine/11tmag-matera-slide-VHKF-copy/11tmag-matera-slide-VHKF-copy-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/11/t-magazine/11tmag-matera-slide-VHKF-copy/11tmag-matera-slide-VHKF-copy-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 667, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/11/t-magazine/11tmag-matera-slide-VHKF-copy/11tmag-matera-slide-VHKF-copy-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 667, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/11/t-magazine/11tmag-matera-slide-VHKF-copy/11tmag-matera-slide-VHKF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/11/t-magazine/11tmag-matera-slide-VHKF-copy/11tmag-matera-slide-VHKF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/11/t-magazine/11tmag-matera-slide-VHKF-copy/11tmag-matera-slide-VHKF-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Where to Stay (and What to Eat) in Matera, Italy', 'kicker': 'Wanderlust', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rock of Ages', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-11T12:29:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'subsection_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Maxwell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Maxwell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d40ae423-3f56-58bc-ae7a-7c1495d7e8c5', 'word_count': 1195, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d40ae423-3f56-58bc-ae7a-7c1495d7e8c5'}, {'abstract': 'In this lesson we invite students to learn about the Roman Empire through stories about the communities that have developed in its wake. From modern Rome to the far reaches of the ancient empire in Syria, they will seek to understand the role that history can play in everyday lives.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/11/learning/lesson-plans/then-and-now-exploring-modern-life-amid-relics-of-the-roman-empire.html', 'snippet': 'In this lesson we invite students to learn about the Roman Empire through stories about the communities that have developed in its wake. From modern Rome to the far reaches of the ancient empire in Syria, they will seek to understand the role that...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Imagine living near the ruins of an ancient culture. Each day offers both delights and challenges, as you witness the ways in which time and modern problems have affected these precious artifacts. What are the costs of protecting these signs of history? And how has daily life changed for people living in such places in the 21st century, at the far end of a timeline reaching back generations?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/10/14/travel/14NEXT7-LN/14NEXT7-LN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/10/14/travel/14NEXT7-LN/14NEXT7-LN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/10/14/travel/14NEXT7-LN/14NEXT7-LN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/10/14/travel/14NEXT7-LN/14NEXT7-LN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/10/14/travel/14NEXT7-LN/14NEXT7-LN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/10/14/travel/14NEXT7-LN/14NEXT7-LN-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/10/14/travel/14NEXT7-LN/14NEXT7-LN-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Then and Now: Exploring Modern Life Amid Relics of the Roman Empire', 'kicker': 'So