T19:05:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Linda Greenhouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Linda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greenhouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b078353-c5ad-5071-b0e7-344b0e67d9ca', 'word_count': 1623, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b078353-c5ad-5071-b0e7-344b0e67d9ca'}, {'abstract': 'Women helped build the movie industry, but it has long been a male-dominated enterprise that systematically treats women — as a class — as inferior.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/11/movies/harvey-weinstein-hollywood.html', 'snippet': 'Women helped build the movie industry, but it has long been a male-dominated enterprise that systematically treats women — as a class — as inferior.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I read the recent allegations that Harvey Weinstein had sexually harassed women for decades, I thought — well, of course. Mr. Weinstein was a famously swaggering bully, and while I hadn’t heard about the specific charges of sexual abuse by women working for him, such behavior fits the movie industry’s pervasive, unrepentant exploitation of women. And then on Tuesday, The New Yorker revealed that three women, including the Italian actress-turned-director Asia Argento, said that “Weinstein raped them.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/12/arts/12WEINSTEIN-INDUSTRY/12WEINSTEIN-INDUSTRY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 833, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/12/arts/12WEINSTEIN-INDUSTRY/12WEINSTEIN-INDUSTRY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 833}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/12/arts/12WEINSTEIN-INDUSTRY/12WEINSTEIN-INDUSTRY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 738, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/12/arts/12WEINSTEIN-INDUSTRY/12WEINSTEIN-INDUSTRY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1476, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/12/arts/12WEINSTEIN-INDUSTRY/12WEINSTEIN-INDUSTRY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/12/arts/12WEINSTEIN-INDUSTRY/12WEINSTEIN-INDUSTRY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/12/arts/12WEINSTEIN-INDUSTRY/12WEINSTEIN-INDUSTRY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Harvey Weinstein Is Gone. But Hollywood Still Has a Problem.', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Weinstein Is Gone. Hollywood Sin Isn’t.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weinstein, Harvey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mayer, Louis B', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miramax Films', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer Inc', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-11T19:19:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb104e45-df35-5d4c-88e9-e8303e8dfe51', 'word_count': 1386, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb104e45-df35-5d4c-88e9-e8303e8dfe51'}, {'abstract': 'No one, including mental health professionals, can predict who will turn violent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/11/opinion/psychiatrists-mass-killers.html', 'snippet': 'No one, including mental health professionals, can predict who will turn violent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the wake of the Las Vegas massacre, politicians are once again promoting the politically expedient notion that better mental health care could stop such mass killings. Paul D. Ryan, the speaker of the House, said last week that “mental health reform is a critical ingredient to making sure that we can try and prevent some of these things from happening in the past.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/12/opinion/12friedmanWeb/12friedmanWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/12/opinion/12friedmanWeb/12friedmanWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/12/opinion/12friedmanWeb/12friedmanWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/12/opinion/12friedmanWeb/12friedmanWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/12/opinion/12friedmanWeb/12friedmanWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/12/opinion/12friedmanWeb/12friedmanWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/12/opinion/12friedmanWeb/12friedmanWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Psychiatrists Can’t Stop Mass Killers', 'kicker': 'Contributing Op-Ed Writer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Psychiatrists Can’t Stop Mass Killers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Las Vegas, Nev, Shooting (October, 2017)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paddock, Stephen C (1953-2017)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychiatry and Psychiatrists', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-11T19:20:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard A. Friedman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Friedman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8624441-4f1b-5e20-b20a-0f8214784687', 'word_count': 742, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8624441-4f1b-5e20-b20a-0f8214784687'}, {'abstract': ' Highlights from the London fairs, which ran last week. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/11/t-magazine/art/frieze-recap.html', 'snippet': ' Highlights from the London fairs, which ran last week. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you’re a mere art lover and not a collector, big art fairs can sometimes make you feel out of sorts. In other words: unwelcome and out of your league. One way to remedy that is to treat them like a museum where you go to look and to learn, rather than to buy. That wasn’t hard to do with London’s contemporary fair, Frieze, and its sister fair Frieze Masters (which features work made before 2000), both of which were last week. Frieze’s organizers make a concerted effort to encourage galleries to go all-out with bespoke booths that promote interactivity — and specially curated sections aimed to provoke or to delight. Here are T’s top picks.  ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/11/t-magazine/art/frieze-slide-ICQP/frieze-slide-ICQP-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/11/t-magazine/art/frieze-slide-ICQP/frieze-slide-ICQP-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/11/t-magazine/art/frieze-slide-ICQP/frieze-slide-ICQP-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/11/t-magazine/art/frieze-slide-ICQP/frieze-slide-ICQP-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/11/t-magazine/art/frieze-slide-ICQP/frieze-slide-ICQP-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/11/t-magazine/art/frieze-slide-ICQP/frieze-slide-ICQP-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/11/t-magazine/art/frieze-slide-ICQP/frieze-slide-ICQP-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '7 Great Things I Saw at Frieze and Frieze Masters', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frieze Art Fair', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-11T19:27:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'subsection_name': 'Art', 'byline': {'original': 'By Laura van Straaten', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e9452389-176b-59fd-90be-85500c20b84c', 'word_count': 1562, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e9452389-176b-59fd-90be-85500c20b84c'}, {'abstract': 'Dr. Jouvet’s research, he wrote, showed that dreaming was “the third state of the brain, as different from sleep as sleep was from waking.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/11/obituaries/michel-jouvet-who-unlocked-rem-sleeps-secrets-dies-at-91.html', 'snippet': 'Dr. Jouvet’s research, he wrote, showed that dreaming was “the third state of the brain, as different from sleep as sleep was from waking.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dr. Michel Jouvet, a neurophysiologist who discovered the region of the brain that controls rapid eye movement, and who helped define REM sleep as a unique state of consciousness common to humans and animals alike, was found dead on Oct. 3 in Villeurbanne, France. He was 91.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/12/obituaries/12jouvet-obit/11jouvet-obit-1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 421, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/12/obituaries/12jouvet-obit/11jouvet-obit-1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 421}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/12/obituaries/12jouvet-obit/11jouvet-obit-1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 719, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/12/obituaries/12jouvet-obit/11jouvet-obit-1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1107, 'width': 1577, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/12/obituaries/12jouvet-obit/11jouvet-obit-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/12/obituaries/12jouvet-obit/11jouvet-obit-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/12/obituaries/12jouvet-obit/11jouvet-obit-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Michel Jouvet, Who Unlocked REM Sleep’s Secrets, Dies at 91', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dr. Michel Jouvet, Pathfinder of REM Sleep, Dies at 91', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jouvet, Michel (1925-2017)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sleep', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Brain', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dreams', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-11T19:29:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Obits', 'section_name': 'Obituaries', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel E. Slotnik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Slotnik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/300bb165-9265-5643-bbfd-84f7fe776d0b', 'word_count': 942, 'uri': 'nyt://article/300bb165-9265-5643-bbfd-84f7fe776d0b'}, {'abstract': 'Labour Party members in Britain also called for an honorary title to be revoked as anger over the scandal spread across Europe.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/11/world/europe/harvey-weinstein-europe.html', 'snippet': 'Labour Party members in Britain also called for an honorary title to be revoked as anger over the scandal spread across Europe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — The sexual abuse scandal surrounding the powerful Hollywood producer Harvey Weinstein has reverberated around the globe, with actors and politicians in Europe condemning his actions and the British film academy suspending his membership on Wednesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 't