'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/12/arts/12robot-recap/12robot-recap-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/12/arts/12robot-recap/12robot-recap-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/12/arts/12robot-recap/12robot-recap-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/12/arts/12robot-recap/12robot-recap-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/12/arts/12robot-recap/12robot-recap-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/12/arts/12robot-recap/12robot-recap-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/12/arts/12robot-recap/12robot-recap-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Mr. Robot’ Season 3 Premiere: A Whole New World', 'kicker': 'Mr. Robot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Mr Robot (TV Program)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-12T03:11:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeremy Egner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Egner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/87f832c8-f1d8-5cf0-8765-e154d4bec564', 'word_count': 1318, 'uri': 'nyt://article/87f832c8-f1d8-5cf0-8765-e154d4bec564'}, {'abstract': 'The creator of the USA techno-thriller discusses the new season, which began on Wednesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/11/arts/television/mr-robot-season-3-premiere-sam-esmail.html', 'snippet': 'The creator of the USA techno-thriller discusses the new season, which began on Wednesday.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Mr. Robot” began as a story about a troubled programmer but steadily expanded to encompass underground revolutionaries, global power brokers and a hack that disrupted the entire world. The USA techno-thriller returned for its third season Wednesday night with even broader horizons, as key characters like Whiterose (B. D. Wong) and Angela Moss (Portia Doubleday) seemed to envision alternate universes, while the tormented hero, Elliot (Rami Malek), resumed his baroque existential struggles. The episode found him recuperating from last season’s culminating gunshot and pondering ways to counteract his Mr. Robot alter ego, specifically his world-shattering acts of cyberterrorism.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/12/arts/television/12robot/12robot-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/12/arts/television/12robot/12robot-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/12/arts/television/12robot/12robot-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/12/arts/television/12robot/12robot-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/12/arts/television/12robot/12robot-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/12/arts/television/12robot/12robot-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/12/arts/television/12robot/12robot-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Mr. Robot’ Season 3 Premiere: Sam Esmail on Parallel Universes and President Trump', 'kicker': 'Ask a Showrunner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Mr. Robot’ Enters a New Sphere', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'USA Network', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Esmail, Sam', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Mr Robot (TV Program)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Malek, Rami (1981- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-12T03:11:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeremy Egner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Egner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interview', '_id': 'nyt://article/d11e5a61-ea7a-5d67-84b9-13dd3acdecab', 'word_count': 1529, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d11e5a61-ea7a-5d67-84b9-13dd3acdecab'}, {'abstract': 'We asked people to share how the wildfires affected them. Here are some of their stories.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/11/us/california-fires-evacuations.html', 'snippet': 'We asked people to share how the wildfires affected them. Here are some of their stories.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Wildfires in California continue to rage, having killed at least 21 people, sent hundreds to the hospital, and damaged or destroyed thousands of buildings. The fires, which started Sunday night, span the length of the state.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Thank God We Left’: Californians Describe Escaping Wildfires', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wildfires', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Evacuations and Evacuees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Napa (Calif)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-12T03:19:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Fahima Haque', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Fahima', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haque', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/71686af5-9374-5010-91ce-a98f8edd1dfd', 'word_count': 910, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71686af5-9374-5010-91ce-a98f8edd1dfd'}, {'abstract': 'There’s so much rumor and muckraking going on, it may be messing with designers’ ability to make good clothes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/12/fashion/fashion-industry-gossip-addiction-paris-fashion-week.html', 'snippet': 'There’s so much rumor and muckraking going on, it may be messing with designers’ ability to make good clothes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fashion has an addiction problem. I am not talking about illicit substances here, though the industry’s past issues with those have been well documented. Rather, I am talking about illicit … well, talk. Gossip. It seems unable to stop, and it is getting worse. In Paris last week there was more leaking going on in the maisons of Avenue Montaigne than in the Trump White House.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/12/fashion/12UNBUTTONED/12UNBUTTONED-articleLarge-v2.gif', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/12/fashion/12UNBUTTONED/12UNBUTTONED-articleLarge-v2.gif', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/12/fashion/12UNBUTTONED/12UNBUTTONED-jumbo-v2.gif', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/12/fashion/12UNBUTTONED/12UNBUTTONED-superJumbo-v2.gif', 'height': 1050, 'width': 1050, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/12/fashion/12UNBUTTONED/12UNBUTTONED-thumbStandard-v2.gif', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/12/fashion/12UNBUTTONED/12UNBUTTONED-thumbStandard-v2.gif', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/12/fashion/12UNBUTTONED/12UNBUTTONED-thumbLarge-v2.gif', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Fashion’s Gossip Addiction', 'kicker': 'Unbuttoned', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gossip Girls (and Boys)', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paris Fashion Week', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gossip', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-12T04:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vanessa Friedman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vanessa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Friedman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/234f5072-3377-5540-921d-d72ff57b7a73', 'word_count': 962, 'uri': 'nyt://article/234f5072-3377-5540-921d-d72ff57b7a73'}, {'abstract': 'Some countries in East Africa, to protect local industries and national pride, have enacted de facto bans of secondhand clothing from abroad. The United States has cried foul.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/12/world/africa/east-africa-rwanda-used-clothing.html', 'snippet': 'Some countries in East Africa, to protect local industries and national pride, have enacted de facto bans of secondhand clothing from abroad. The United States has cried foul.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KIGALI, Rwanda — In Kenya, they are called the “clothes of dead white people.” In Mozambique, they are the “clothing of calamity.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4',