rticle/3acb0936-8a88-50f3-ad3d-3f284beee720'}, {'abstract': 'Representatives Al Green, Democrat of Texas, released on Wednesday articles of impeachment against President Trump.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2017/10/12/us/politics/document-Read-Al-Green-s-Impeachment-Resolution.html', 'snippet': 'Representatives Al Green, Democrat of Texas, released on Wednesday articles of impeachment against President Trump.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Representatives Al Green, Democrat of Texas, released on Wednesday articles of impeachment against President Trump.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/11/us/politics/image-Read-Al-Green-s-Impeachment-Resolution/image-Read-Al-Green-s-Impeachment-Resolution-articleLarge.gif', 'height': 776, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/11/us/politics/image-Read-Al-Green-s-Impeachment-Resolution/image-Read-Al-Green-s-Impeachment-Resolution-articleLarge.gif', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 776}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/11/us/politics/image-Read-Al-Green-s-Impeachment-Resolution/image-Read-Al-Green-s-Impeachment-Resolution-jumbo.gif', 'height': 1024, 'width': 792, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/11/us/politics/image-Read-Al-Green-s-Impeachment-Resolution/image-Read-Al-Green-s-Impeachment-Resolution-superJumbo.gif', 'height': 1294, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/11/us/politics/image-Read-Al-Green-s-Impeachment-Resolution/image-Read-Al-Green-s-Impeachment-Resolution-thumbStandard.gif', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/11/us/politics/image-Read-Al-Green-s-Impeachment-Resolution/image-Read-Al-Green-s-Impeachment-Resolution-thumbStandard.gif', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/11/us/politics/image-Read-Al-Green-s-Impeachment-Resolution/image-Read-Al-Green-s-Impeachment-Resolution-thumbLarge.gif', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': "Read Al Green's Resolution to Impeach Donald Trump", 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2017-10-12T09:00:25+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'U.S.', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/b956f4c2-199c-52fa-a232-1b65f2940997', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/b956f4c2-199c-52fa-a232-1b65f2940997'}, {'abstract': 'The restaurant favorite is just as easy to make at home.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/12/magazine/cooking-duck-not-with-love-but-with-pleasure.html', 'snippet': 'The restaurant favorite is just as easy to make at home.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With some frequency these days, you’ll hear talk of cooking “with love” — that supposed secret ingredient, the intangible something extra that makes a chef’s food so good. I am sure that is accurate for some, but I imagine that what is identified as love is probably thoroughness and follow-through and taking the time that work-done-properly takes. What you unfortunately don’t get to hear very often (unless you work in kitchens) is how sharp and droll and cynical and pragmatic chefs can be too. I’m not saying you can taste it in the food, but every kitchen everywhere has a charming and agreeable dose of jadedness — a vaguely begrudging eye roll expressed most commonly when it comes to menu-planning time in the observation “You could throw your grandmother on the grill with goat cheese and artichokes and sell a thousand plates a night.”', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/15/magazine/15eat-copy/15mag-15eat-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/15/magazine/15eat-copy/15mag-15eat-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/15/magazine/15eat-copy/15mag-15eat-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/15/magazine/15eat-copy/15mag-15eat-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/15/magazine/15eat-copy/15mag-15eat-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/15/magazine/15eat-copy/15mag-15eat-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/15/magazine/15eat-copy/15mag-15eat-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cooking Duck Not With Love but With Pleasure', 'kicker': 'Eat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cooking Like a Cynic', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ducks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-12T09:00:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gabrielle Hamilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gabrielle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hamilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/72437d77-f044-55b3-a1ce-f40e90c3a2b4', 'word_count': 1049, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72437d77-f044-55b3-a1ce-f40e90c3a2b4'}, {'abstract': 'Proposed mines near the Boundary Waters have become the latest front in the fight over who gets to profit from America’s natural resources.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/12/magazine/in-northern-minnesota-two-economies-square-off-mining-vs-wilderness.html', 'snippet': 'Proposed mines near the Boundary Waters have become the latest front in the fight over who gets to profit from America’s natural resources.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Minnesota is home to some of the world’s most ancient rocks, as old as 3.5 billion years. Earth has been around for only 4.5 billion years. About 2.7 billion years ago, basalt lava flowed underwater near what’s now the state’s border with Canada; the lava hardened, and the creep of geologic time turned it into a bedrock of greenstone and granite. On top of it, a layer of sedimentary rock rich in iron ore formed nearly two billion years ago, when the region was ocean floor. Then a billion years ago, Earth’s crust cracked open, producing a 50-mile-wide fissure stretching from Lake Superior to Kansas. For the next 100 million years, lava bubbled up into what geologists call the Midcontinent Rift, forming a mineral deposit filled with copper and nickel. Settlers first made their way to the area in 1865 in a fruitless search for gold. What they did find was iron ore, and lots of it. Rails were laid for iron-ore transport, and the town of Ely was founded a few years later, in 1888.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '32', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/15/magazine/15boundary1/15mag-15boundary-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/15/magazine/15boundary1/15mag-15boundary-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/15/magazine/15boundary1/15mag-15boundary-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/15/magazine/15boundary1/15mag-15boundary-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1535, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/15/magazine/15boundary1/15boundary1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/15/magazine/15boundary1/15boundary1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/15/magazine/15boundary1/15boundary1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Northern Minnesota, Two Economies Square Off: Mining vs. Wilderness', 'kicker': 'Feature', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Water War', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mines and Mining', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wilderness Areas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Land Use Policies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Geology', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boundary Waters Canoe Area (Minn)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Minnesota', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-12T09:00:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Reid Forgrave', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Reid', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Forgrave', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c441a347-bc3d-573c-88fb-06503bced50b', 'word_count': 4581, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c441a347-bc3d-573c-88fb-06503bced50b'}, {'abstract': 'Goya, Rembrandt and van Gogh (for starters) lead the Thaw collection at the Morgan, one of the great troves of treasured drawings.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/12/arts/design/a-gathering-of-greats-in-a-trove-of-drawings-at-the-morgan.html', 'snippet': 'Goya, Rembrandt and van Gogh (for starters) lead the Thaw collection at the Morgan, one of the great troves of treasured drawings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Item by luminous, brain-zapping item, “Drawn to Greatness: Master Drawings From the Thaw Collection” at the Morgan Library & Museum has to be one of the paramount group drawing shows of the era. It is also a grand summing-up of a c