evere than the Depression.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'We’re About to Fall Behind the Great Depression', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Great Depression (1930's)", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inflation (Economics)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-12T11:31:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Leonhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leonhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e78a9b5-06db-5679-8b25-9a89b2140743', 'word_count': 631, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e78a9b5-06db-5679-8b25-9a89b2140743'}, {'abstract': 'This was the Yankees’ bonus year, when nobody thought they would win very much — maybe not even the players. How could we all see this coming?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/12/sports/baseball/new-york-yankees-cleveland-indians.html', 'snippet': 'This was the Yankees’ bonus year, when nobody thought they would win very much — maybe not even the players. How could we all see this coming?', 'lead_paragraph': 'CLEVELAND — You get one chance, just one, for a season like this in New York. Once a group wins, that becomes the expectation. It is like a first kiss: Everything changes, and there is no going back.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/13/sports/13kepnerWEB1/13kepnerWEB1