html', 'snippet': 'A documentary by Alexandre O. Philippe finds plenty to examine in one of the most memorable scenes in American film.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2000, the critic Andrew Sarris, one of the original champions of “Psycho,” wrote of how a student had spotted a hidden meaning in Hitchcock’s editing of a scene with Sheriff Chambers (John McIntire). He credited the student with having given him a fresh eye on a film he thought he knew backward and forward.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/13/arts/1378-52HITCHCOCK/1378-52HITCHCOCK-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 316, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/13/arts/1378-52HITCHCOCK/1378-52HITCHCOCK-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 316}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/13/arts/1378-52HITCHCOCK/1378-52HITCHCOCK-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 540, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/13/arts/1378-52HITCHCOCK/1378-52HITCHCOCK-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1080, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/13/arts/1378-52HITCHCOCK/1378-52HITCHCOCK-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/13/arts/1378-52HITCHCOCK/1378-52HITCHCOCK-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/13/arts/1378