 — a Nashville landmark saturated with decades of burger grease — she settled for unsweetened iced tea. Sensing the waitress’s displeasure, the singer-songwriter known for her lusty honky-tonk sound briefly contemplated ordering a meal for the sake of appearances. “We’ll leave a large tip,” she said, adding an apology.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/15/arts/15MARGOPRICE1/15MARGOPRICE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/15/arts/15MARGOPRICE1/15MARGOPRICE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/15/arts/15MARGOPRICE1/15MARGOPRICE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/15/arts/15MARGOPRICE1/15MARGOPRICE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/15/arts/15MARGOPRICE1/15MARGOPRICE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/15/arts/15MARGOPRICE1/15MARGOPRICE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/15/arts/15MARGOPRICE1/15MARGOPRICE1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Margo Price, Nashville Outsider, Tells It Like It Really Is', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘The Struggle Is Who I Am’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Country Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'All American Made (Album)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Price, Margo', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-12T12:23:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jewly Hight', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jewly', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hight', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ae4b162-ce66-512a-b297-61e00899c17b', 'word_count': 1701, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ae4b162-ce66-512a-b297-61e00899c17b'}, {'abstract': 'A documentary observes a St. Louis student facing a bleak future if she can’t graduate from an alternative school.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/12/movies/review-in-for-ahkeem-a-last-option-for-a-troubled-teenager.html', 'snippet': 'A documentary observes a St. Louis student facing a bleak future if she can’t graduate from an alternative school.', 'lead_paragraph': '“For Ahkeem,” a documentary directed by Jeremy S. Levine and Landon Van Soest, grew out of a People magazine article from 2011 about the Innovative Concept Academy, an alternative school in St. Louis designed to rehabilitate teenagers who might otherwise be incarcerated. The film follows one such student over about two years.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/13/arts/13forahkeem/13forahkeem-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'le