 'lead_paragraph': 'Ben Shapiro, the conservative writer, prides himself on speaking bold truths to liberal power. His shtick goes something like this: Set up a speech in a progressive bastion, ideally a college campus full of coastal elites who have never left their bubble. Spar with snowflakes who are offended by something he says about race or gender and perhaps even believe he never should have been invited in the first place. Post the exchange on the internet and use it as proof that the cultural consensus is stacked dramatically against conservatives. As Mr. Shapiro has put it: “The left has run out of aggressors to target; instead, they’ve become the aggressors, self-righteous morality police dedicated to wiping out dissenting thought.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/12/opinion/12coastonWeb/12coastonWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/12/opinion/12coastonWeb/12coastonWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/12/opinion/12coastonWeb/12coastonWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/12/opinion/12coastonWeb/12coastonWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/12/opinion/12coastonWeb/12coastonWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/12/opinion/12coastonWeb/12coastonWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/12/opinion/12coastonWeb/12coastonWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Hollow Bravery of Ben Shapiro', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Domenech, Ben (1981- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hemingway, Mollie Ziegler', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-12T14:45:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jane Coaston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Coaston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c485fbf-1144-5e3d-bc32-fcc98bb1efbc', 'word_count': 1076, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c485fbf-1144-5e3d-bc32-fcc98bb1efbc'}, {'abstract': 'The Israeli government’s hard-line tactics have found their way to the United States. Can the Constitution stop them?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/12/opinion/israel-congress-bds.html', 'snippet': 'The Israeli government’s hard-line tactics have found their way to the United States. Can the Constitution stop them?', 'lead_paragraph': 'For decades, I’ve supported activists working toward democracy and equality in Israel. But in the past eight years under Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu, that fight has become much more difficult. Bills we once thought the Knesset would never allow to be even introduced are now the law of the land. This crackdown has included the entrenchment of Israel’s occupation of Palestinian territories, but also government support for McCarthy-like witch hunts of undesirable progressive activists — many of which have targeted the New Israel Fund, the organization I lead, and the progressive Israeli nonprofits we fund.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/12/opinion/12sokatchWeb/12sokatchWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 408, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/12/opinion/12sokatchWeb/12sokatchWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 408}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/12/opinion/12sokatchWeb/12sokatchWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 696, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/12/opinion/12sokatchWeb/12sokatchWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1391, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/12/opinion/12sokatchWeb/12sokatchWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/12/opinion/12sokatchWeb/12sokatchWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/12/opinion/12sokatchWeb/12sokatchWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Congress’s Un-American, Bad-for-Israel Agenda', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'American Civil Liberties Union', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Israeli Settlements', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boycotts', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-12T14:50:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel Sokatch', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sokatch', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/46463756-2b23-5482-aaff-fe895ec58728', 'word_count': 892, 'uri': 'nyt://article/46463756-2b23-5482-aaff-fe895ec58728'}, {'abstract': 'The Chiefs look to remain perfect, while the Jaguars hope to quit their Jekyll and Hyde routine. Here are our picks against the spread.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/12/sports/nfl-predictions-schedule.html', 'snippet': 'The Chiefs look to remain perfect, while the Jaguars hope to quit their Jekyll and Hyde routine. Here are our picks against the spread.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The pecking order in the N.F.L. is starting to emerge. The Chiefs, Packers and Panthers are right at the top, with the Eagles, Lions, Patriots and Falcons looming just behind them. Stuck somewhere between “best team in the N.F.L.” and “totally incompetent” are the Jacksonville Jaguars. Their Jekyll and Hyde season has gone W-L-W-L-W, and they managed the nearly impossible feat of losing to the Jets in Week 4 and then completely demoralizing the Steelers in Week 5. Their pendulum could continue to swing, but maybe, just maybe, they can win a second game in a row. Here are our picks against the spread.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/11/sports/15nflpreview-jaguars/15nflpreview-jaguars-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 358, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/11/sports/15nflpreview-jaguars/15nflpreview-jaguars-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 358}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/11/sports/15nflpreview-jaguars/15nflpreview-jaguars-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 610, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/11/sports/15nflpreview-jaguars/15nflpreview-jaguars-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1221, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/11/sports/15nflpreview-jaguars/15nflpreview-jaguars-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/11/sports/15nflpreview-jaguars/15nflpreview-jaguars-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/11/sports/15nflpreview-jaguars/15nflpreview-jaguars-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'N.F.L. Week 6 Picks: Chiefs Over Steelers; Packers Over Vikings', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jaguars Look for a Rarity: Two Wins in a Row', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jacksonville Jaguars', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Rams', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ramsey, Jalen (1994- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kansas City Chiefs', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Green Bay Packers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Carolina Panthers', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-12T14:53:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Hoffman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoffman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ee4ebd3-8721-5c2b-9395-8ba1e3d99bac', 'word_count': 2078, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ee4ebd3-8721-5c2b-9395-8ba1e3d99bac'}, {'abstract': 'Poor play derailed the team after it led the Yankees in the division series, two games to none, and after a regular season featuring 102 wins and a 22-game win streak.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/12/sports/baseball/cleveland-indians-playoffs.html', 'snippet': 'Poor play derailed the team after it led the Yankees in the division series, two games to none, and after a regular season featuring 102 wins and a 22-game win streak.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CLEVELAND — When this latest sad volume of Cleveland Indians history is written, bound and placed on a shelf alongside all the others, the 2017 team will be remembered for two notable streaks: the 22 consecutive games it won in August and September, and the three in a row it lost in October.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/13/sports/13indians1/13indians1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 320, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/13/sports/13indians1/13indians1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 320}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/13/sports/13indians1/13indians1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 546, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/13/sports/13indians1/13indians1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1092, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/13/sports/13indians1/13indians1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/13/sports/13indians1/13indians1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/13/sports/13indians1/13indians1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Happened to the Cleveland Indians?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What Happened to the Mighty Indians?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cleveland Indians', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Allen, Cody (1988- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Francona, Terry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-12T14:54:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d51bc4f-1a21-5b1f-bdc4-20fe5bebb425', 'word_count': 966, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d51bc4f-1a21-5b1f-bdc4-20fe5bebb425'}, {'abstract': 'And: the friend who won’t wash his hands after using the bathroom; sharing one’s rape story with a boyfriend; the old “throw out some dates” gambit.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/12/style/what-happens-when-a-will-is-unsigned.html', 'snippet': 'And: the friend who won’t wash his hands after using the bathroom; sharing one’s rape story with a boyfriend; the old “throw out some dates” gambit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My Uncle Eddy died unexpectedly. He never married and had no children, but he was very close to my brother and his wife. Eddy spent every occasion with them. He wrote a will leaving them everything but never signed it. Under state law, our lawyer says, Eddy’s property will be split among his three siblings, none of whom spoke to him. Eddy was tough. My brother and his wife were the only ones who could take his tirades. But they loved him. One of Eddy’s siblings will honor the unsigned will; the others want their money. Help our divided family!', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 599, 'width': 600,