 'persons', 'value': 'Schiller, Bob (1918-2017)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'I Love Lucy (TV Program)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'ALL IN THE FAMILY (TV PROGRAM)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Maude (TV Program)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-12T19:11:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Obits', 'section_name': 'Obituaries', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/26dfe733-3a13-526e-8292-eb3a81fbe797', 'word_count': 1014, 'uri': 'nyt://article/26dfe733-3a13-526e-8292-eb3a81fbe797'}, {'abstract': 'The organization is framing a cynical business strategy as a progressive step forward. Don’t fall for it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/12/opinion/boy-scouts-girls-.html', 'snippet': 'The organization is framing a cynical business strategy as a progressive step forward. Don’t fall for it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The news arrived on Oct. 11, a day — as Facebook reminded us — designated as the International Day of the Girl. On the surface, it even seemed like it might be a progressive change: The Boy Scouts of America announced that it would allow girls to participate in Cub Scouts and to eventually earn Eagle Scout rank.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/13/opinion/13tuttle/13tuttle-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/13/opinion/13tuttle/13tuttle-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/13/opinion/13tuttle/13tuttle-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/13/opinion/13tuttle/13tuttle-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/13/opinion/13tuttle/13tuttle-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/13/opinion/13tuttle/13tuttle-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/13/opinion/13tuttle/13tuttle-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Girls, Don’t Become Boy Scouts', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Girls, Don’t Become Boy Scouts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boy Scouts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Girl Scouts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conservatism (US Politics)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-12T19:15:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Tuttle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tuttle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1d8be95-5789-5ed8-8aeb-b7bd64c9e606', 'word_count': 753, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1d8be95-5789-5ed8-8aeb-b7bd64c9e606'}, {'abstract': 'The night before their release was announced, President Trump teased the pending freedom of an American woman and her family who were held hostage for five years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/12/us/politics/trump-militants-hostage-release.html', 'snippet': 'The night before their release was announced, President Trump teased the pending freedom of an American woman and her family who were held hostage for five years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — He was talking taxes with truckers on Wednesday evening when President Trump suddenly diverged into a curious tangent. He had been given “some very, very important news” that “you’ll probably be hearing about” in the next few days. What it was, he did not say.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/13/us/13dc-prexy1/13dc-prexy1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/13/us/13dc-prexy1/13dc-prexy1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/13/us/13dc-prexy1/13dc-prexy1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/13/us/13dc-prexy1/13dc-prexy1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subTyp