_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/c62ad209-75a8-540f-a97d-7db167125f5a', 'word_count': 495, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c62ad209-75a8-540f-a97d-7db167125f5a'}, {'abstract': 'Our guide to the city’s best classical music and opera.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/12/arts/music/classical-music-in-nyc-this-week.html', 'snippet': 'Our guide to the city’s best classical music and opera.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THOMAS ADÈS AND FRIENDS at Zankel Hall (Oct. 15, 3 p.m.). Thomas Adès is in New York for the buildup to the Metropolitan Opera’s performances of “The Exterminating Angel,” but here we find him as an accompanist for an afternoon of songs. Sally Matthews, Alice Coote, Iestyn Davies and Joseph Kaiser are the vocalists for works by Purcell (many of them transcribed by Mr. Adès), Schubert, Britten, Woolrich, Stravinsky and the composer-conductor-pianist himself.212-247-7800, carnegiehall.org', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/13/arts/13LISTINGS-CLASSICAL/13LISTINGS-CLASSICAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 422, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/13/arts/13LISTINGS-CLASSICAL/13LISTINGS-CLASSICAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 422}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/13/arts/13LISTINGS-CLASSICAL/13LISTINGS-CLASSICAL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 720, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/13/arts/13LISTINGS-CLASSICAL/13LISTINGS-CLASSICAL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1441, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credi