rm for modest swimwear favored by many religious women — would be banned from the city’s beaches; a municipal official called the bathing suits “ostentatious clothing” expressing an “allegiance to terrorist movements that are at war with us.”', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/15/opinion/sunday/15polakow-suransky/15polakow-suransky-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 449, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/15/opinion/sunday/15polakow-suransky/15polakow-suransky-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 449}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/15/opinion/sunday/15polakow-suransky/15polakow-suransky-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 766, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/15/opinion/sunday/15polakow-suransky/15polakow-suransky-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1459, 'width': 1951, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/15/opinion/sunday/15polakow-suransky/15polakow-suransky-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/15/opinion/sunday/15polakow-suransky/15polakow-suransky-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/15/opinion/sunday/15polakow-suransky/15polakow-suransky-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'White Nationalism Is Destroying the West', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'White Nationalism Is the Real Existential Threat to the West. Not Jihad.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refugees and Displaced Persons', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Whites', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fringe Groups and Movements', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-12T20:44:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sasha Polakow-Suransky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sasha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Polakow-Suransky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d877ce5-b316-5aaa-a7f0-60374027781e', 'word_count': 1868, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d877ce5-b316-5aaa-a7f0-60374027781e'}, {'abstract': 'Our guide to dance performances.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/12/arts/dance/dance-in-nyc-this-week.html', 'snippet': 'Our guide to dance performances.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AMERICAN BALLET THEATER at the David H. Koch Theater, Lincoln Center (Oct. 18-29, at various times). American Ballet Theater’s director, Kevin McKenzie, has said that one of his best moves in 25 years of leadership was hiring Alexei Ratmansky as choreographer-in-residence. This gala on Wednesday celebrates Mr. McKenzie’s quarter-century on the job and features the premiere of “Songs of Bukovina” by Mr. Ratmansky. Mr. McKenzie has also championed the choreographer Jessica Lang, who contributes a new work and whose previous company commission, “Her Notes,” is on Thursday’s program along with Mr. Ratmansky’s “Serenade After Plato’s Symposium,” Jerome Robbins’s “Other Dances” and Frederick Ashton’s “Symphonic Variations.” 212-496-0600, abt.org', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/13/arts/13LISTINGS-DANCE/13LISTINGS-DANCE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 394, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/13/arts/13LISTINGS-DANCE/13LISTINGS-DANCE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 394}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/13/arts/13LISTINGS-DANCE/13LISTINGS-DANCE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 673, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/13/arts/13LISTINGS-DANCE/13LISTINGS-DANCE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1345, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/13/arts/13LISTINGS-DANCE/13LISTINGS-DANCE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/13/arts/13LISTINGS-DANCE/13LISTINGS-DANCE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/13/arts/13LISTINGS