', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cfbaa297-a1ee-5238-b79f-af26967c68a0', 'word_count': 1102, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cfbaa297-a1ee-5238-b79f-af26967c68a0'}, {'abstract': 'More than just “The Handmaid’s Tale,” the streaming service has loads of old and new series that may have slipped your attention.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/13/watching/great-hulu-tv-shows-underseeen.html', 'snippet': 'More than just “The Handmaid’s Tale,” the streaming service has loads of old and new series that may have slipped your attention.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thanks to “The Handmaid’s Tale,” which last year became the first streaming-service original series to win an Emmy for best drama, some of you may be subscribing to Hulu for the first time and wondering how to get your money’s worth (and if you’re still not sure whether to subscribe, here’s our guide to the streaming service.) Much of Hulu’s TV content consists of current, widely seen shows, but the streaming service has also licensed a handful of old and new series — in a variety of genres — that even dedicated telephiles may have missed. Here are a handful worth digging into:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/10/watching/selfie-watching/selfie-watching-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/10/watching/selfie-watching/selfie-watching-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/10/watching/selfie-watching/selfie-watching-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/10/w