ay around with us, but we’re not scared.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/14/crosswords/variety-acrostic.html', 'snippet': 'Emily Cox and Henry Rathvon play around with us, but we’re not scared.', 'lead_paragraph': 'VARIETY PUZZLE — Fear, or the lack of it, is such a great subject for a column about puzzle solving. Fear can hold people back in many facets of their lives, but it’s especially true when it comes to learning to solve puzzles. For some reason, many people have surprisingly little faith in their abilities, and I wish I could convince them that they know so much more than they think they do and can do so much more than they believe they can.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Variety: Acrostic', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Acrostic Puzzles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tyler, Aisha (1970- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-14T16:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Games', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/485d9e71-1a45-535c-a265-5e7edf9ac637', 'word_count': 297, 'uri': 'nyt://article/485d9e71-1a45-535c-a265-5e7edf9ac637'}, {'abstract': 'The nation has seen Mr. Corker, a reliable Republican senator from a deep-red state, stunningly undermining his president. Chattanooga has seen it coming, for better or worse.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/14/us/politics/back-home-a-unanimous-verdict-on-corker-vs-trump-thats-just-bob.html', 'snippet': 'The nation has seen Mr. C