': None, 'lastname': 'Wang', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/152ab0d4-cad1-5243-99cd-739d8bff89c8', 'word_count': 530, 'uri': 'nyt://article/152ab0d4-cad1-5243-99cd-739d8bff89c8'}, {'abstract': 'The fire took our family’s house. And reminded us that everything is temporary.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/14/opinion/sunday/california-fires-napa.html', 'snippet': 'The fire took our family’s house. And reminded us that everything is temporary.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first time my family’s hillside house in Napa, Calif., burned to the ground, it was 1960 and my father was 14 years old. Everyone escaped in a pickup truck, bringing little more than a handful of pictures and the clothes on their backs. “Being novices, we took all the wrong things,” my uncle remembers. “We grabbed lamps and blenders instead of photographs.” The next day, mostly everything was gone. The hill was charred earth and black trees.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/15/opinion/sunday/15ljohnson/15ljohnson-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/15/opinion/sunday/15ljohnson/15ljohnson-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/15/opinion/sunday/15ljohnson/15ljohnson-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/15/opinion/sunday/15ljohnson/15ljohnson-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/15/opinion/sunday/15ljohnson/15ljohnson-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/15/opinion/sunday/15ljohnson/15ljohnson-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/15/opinion/sunday/15ljohnson/15ljohnson-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Ashes in Napa', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Ashes in Napa', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Napa (Calif)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wildfires', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-14T18:30:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lindsey Lee Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lindsey', 'middlename': 'Lee', 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/292b54a5-f9a3-5e81-9510-586a8538c899', 'word_count': 1081, 'uri': 'nyt://article/292b54a5-f9a3-5e81-9510-586a8538c899'}, {'abstract': 'I loved acting. But I didn’t realize what it was to be taken seriously until I began directing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/14/opinion/sunday/harvey-weinstein-sarah-polley.html', 'snippet': 'I loved acting. But I didn’t realize what it was to be taken seriously until I began directing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One day, when I was 19 years old, I was in the middle of a photo shoot for a Miramax film when I was suddenly told it was time to leave. I was wearing a little black dress, showing a lot of cleavage, lying seductively on my side and looking slyly at the camera. The part I had played in the movie, “Guinevere,” could not have been more removed from this pose. My character was an awkward girl, bumbling, in fact, who wore sweatshirts and jeans, and had little sense of her sexual power. But this was how they were going to sell the movie, and at a certain point, I was tired of being a problem, which is how a female actor is invariably treated whenever she points out that she is being objectified or not respected.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/15/opinion/sunday/15Polley/15Polley-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/15/opinion/sunday/15Polley/15Polley-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/15/opinion/sunday/15Polley/15Polley-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/15/opinion/sunday/15Polley/15Polley-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1362, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/15/opinion/sunday/15Polley/15Polley-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/15/opinion/sunday/15Polley/1