sia in 1917. I was.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the house on the corner, past the cigarette kiosk and the laundry place and the twisted metal barricade assembled to shield passers-by from gunfire, I pitched in with a group of kids carrying rocks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/16/opinion/16redcenturyweb/16shenkerWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 790, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/16/opinion/16redcenturyweb/16shenkerWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 790}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/16/opinion/16redcenturyweb/16shenkerWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 778, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/16/opinion/16redcenturyweb/16shenkerWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1556, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/16/opinion/16redcenturyweb/16shenkerWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/16/opinion/16redcenturyweb/16shenkerWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/16/opinion/16redcenturyweb/16shenkerWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Journalist and the Revolution', 'kicker': 'Red Century', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None,