 the Belarus Free Theater and the Freedom Theater explore the drama of confronting authority.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No matter what the laws of physics decree, there is untold and explosive energy in resistance. Or such is the evidence of “Burning Doors,” the Belarus Free Theater’s bruising exploration of the dynamics of resistance — the kind that occurs in the intersection of art and politics — at La MaMa.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/18/arts/18SIEGE-NOTEBOOK1/18SIEGE-NOTEBOOK1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 429, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/18/arts/18SIEGE-NOTEBOOK1/18SIEGE-NOTEBOOK1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 429}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/18/arts/18SIEGE-NOTEBOOK1/18SIEGE-NOTEBOOK1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 733, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/18/arts/18SIEGE-NOTEBOOK1/18SIEGE-NOTEBOOK1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1465, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/18/arts/18SIEGE-NOTEBOOK1/18SIEGE-NOTEBOOK1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/18/arts/18SIEGE-NOTEBOOK1/18SIEGE-NOTEBOOK1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/18/arts/18SIEGE-NOTEBOOK1/18SIEGE-NOTEBOOK1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'w