an Unlikely Place: Fact-Checking Sites', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Google Serves Fake News Ads  On Fact-Check Sites (Really)', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rumors and Misinformation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Online Advertising', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search Engines', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'PolitiFact.com', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Snopes', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-17T19:36:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daisuke Wakabayashi and Linda Qiu', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daisuke', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wakabayashi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Linda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Qiu', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4f1c1adb-fc77-526d-97cd-48526e0c4ce6', 'word_count': 1233, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4f1c1adb-fc77-526d-97cd-48526e0c4ce6'}, {'abstract': 'The University of Wisconsin’s anti-protest policy shows it’s more worried about protecting conservative opinions than student expression.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/17/opinion/conservatives-campus-speech-wisconsin.html', 'snippet': 'The University of Wisconsin’s anti-protest policy shows it’s more worried about protecting conservative opinions than student expression.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I only remember a little of what I learned during my first days as a University of Wisconsin-Madison freshman in the late 1990s. The vegetarian chili sold in the student union’s bar tasted of beans and sawdust. The most important unwritten rule required freshmen to take blurry Polaroid pictures of ourselves seated atop the lap of the Abraham Lincoln statue at 2 a.m. And if we wanted to protest anything, we could.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/17/opinion/17cauleyWeb/17cauleyWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/17/opinion/17cauleyWeb/17cauleyWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/17/opinion/17cauleyWeb/17cauleyWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/17/opinion/17cauleyWeb/17cauleyWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/17/opinion/17cauleyWeb/17cauleyWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/17/opinion/17cauleyWeb/17cauleyWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/17/opinion/17cauleyWeb/17cauleyWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When Conservatives Suppress Campus Speech', 'kicker': 'On Campus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Wisconsin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Madison (Wis)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-17T19:50:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kashana Cauley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kashana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cauley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd8e1c2f-daa0-5601-888e-d43ad7fe3381', 'word_count': 733, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd8e1c2f-daa0-5601-888e-d43ad7fe3381'}, {'abstract': 'Reggie Jackson has been keeping a watchful eye on Judge and thinks the young Yankee slugger needs the benefit of more major league at-bats.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/17/sports/baseball/aaron-judge-yankees.html', 'snippet': 'Reggie Jackson has been keeping a watchful eye on Judge and thinks the young Yankee slugger needs the benefit of more major league at-bats.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Reggie Jackson watched on Monday as Aaron Judge ripped impressive batting-practice rockets into the farthest reaches of Yankee Stadium. All the while, Mr. October was explaining why pitches that dart low and outside should, in theory, present excellent opportunities for a power hitter.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption'