y Awards', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lithgow, John', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Mikado (Opera)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Crown (TV Program)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-18T02:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Games', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb391e2b-9e0c-54c2-b1a6-cc2c4baad46d', 'word_count': 918, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb391e2b-9e0c-54c2-b1a6-cc2c4baad46d'}, {'abstract': 'The Emmy Award-winning actor John Lithgow on adding “crossword puzzle constructor” to his list of accomplishments.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/17/crosswords/john-lithgow-is-not-eldritch.html', 'snippet': 'The Emmy Award-winning actor John Lithgow on adding “crossword puzzle constructor” to his list of accomplishments.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WEDNESDAY PUZZLE — The Emmy-award winning actor John Lithgow does not have a favorite word, he says, because he loves too many of them to narrow the choice down to a single one. When pressed, he comes up with “eldritch,” an intriguing word that means sinister and eerie, and which seems to have made a kind of comeback in the 20th century. It is exactly the type of word that a logophile like Mr. Lithgow might like, and he savors it as it leaves his lips.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/18/crosswords/18lithgowquigley/18lithgowquigley-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 333, 'width': 384, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None