: None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba028c1b-bdb0-5047-b784-65d446f5997b', 'word_count': 1914, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba028c1b-bdb0-5047-b784-65d446f5997b'}, {'abstract': 'The activist on the intersection of faith and politics and the importance of white protesters in Charlottesville.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/18/magazine/bree-newsome-thinks-allies-should-be-protesting.html', 'snippet': 'The activist on the intersection of faith and politics and the importance of white protesters in Charlottesville.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s been a little over two years since you removed a Confederate flag from the flagpole on the grounds of the South Carolina statehouse. Are you surprised that we’re still having a debate over monuments to the Confederacy? Is it possible to not be surprised in retrospect? There was a point when it was shocking — maybe a year and a half ago, as I saw the ascendance of Donald Trump. But looking back, it makes sense to me that, given the history of America, there would be this backlash that accompanies the election of the first black president.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '58', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/22/magazine/22talk-promo/22talk-promo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/22/magazine/22talk-promo/22talk-promo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/22/magazine/22talk-promo/22talk-promo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/22/magazine/22talk-promo/22talk-promo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/22/magazine/22talk-promo/22talk-promo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/22/magazine/22talk-promo/22talk-promo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/22/magazine/22talk-promo/22talk-promo-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bree Newsome Thinks Allies Should Be Protesting', 'kicker': 'Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bree Newsome Thinks Allies Should Be Protesting', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Byuarim-Newsome, Brittany Ann (1985- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Charlottesville, Va, Violence (August, 2017)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Charlottesville (Va)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Flags, Emblems and Insignia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-18T09:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'Interview by Ana Marie Cox', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Interview', 'middlename': 'Ana', 'lastname': 'Marie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3339f11-3341-5e69-8c63-0b54aec8ddd1', 'word_count': 669, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3339f11-3341-5e69-8c63-0b54aec8ddd1'}, {'abstract': 'As a young social psychologist, she played by the rules and won big: an influential study, a viral TED talk, a prestigious job at Harvard. Then, suddenly, the rules changed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/18/magazine/when-the-revolution-came-for-amy-cuddy.html', 'snippet': 'As a young social psychologist, she played by the rules and won big: an influential study, a viral TED talk, a prestigious job at Harvard. Then, suddenly, the rules changed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I first met Amy Cuddy in January, soon after she moved into a new office at the Harvard School of Public Health. Cuddy was, at the time, officially on the faculty at Harvard Business School, but she was taking a temporary leave, her small box of an office filled with boxes. As she talked about her life in recent years, my attention kept drifting to her left arm, which she had trapped underneath her right leg, which crossed the left. She was slightly hunched over, and yet her right arm, long and lean — she danced for many years — gesticulated freely and expressively, so that the contrast gave the impression of someone in a conflicted emotional state, someone both wanting to tell her story and unsure about doing so.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/22/magazine/22cover/22cover-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 703, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/22/magazine/22cover/22cover-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 703}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/22/magazine/22cover/22cover-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 875, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name':