anization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c21566c-f3d1-53ce-a90f-fc45592de9f3', 'word_count': 664, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c21566c-f3d1-53ce-a90f-fc45592de9f3'}, {'abstract': 'President Xi Jinping of China gave a 205-minute speech to open the Communist Party congress. Here is what mattered.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/18/world/asia/china-xi-jinping-party-congress.html', 'snippet': 'President Xi Jinping of China gave a 205-minute speech to open the Communist Party congress. Here is what mattered.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — As Xi Jinping’s first five-year term as China’s leader ends, he gave himself a shining report card on Wednesday — and a big to-do list for his next five years. Speaking at the start of a Communist Party congress in Beijing, Mr. Xi gave a work report that summed up his achievements so far, while also laying out where he wants to take China in his second term, which starts after this congress. Sitting on a podium before 2,300 delegates, he spoke for 205 minutes, long enough that his predecessor, Hu Jintao, pointed at his watch when Mr. Xi finally finished.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/19/world/19china-takeaways-1/19china-takeaways-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/19/world/19china-takeaways-1/19china-takeaways-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/19/world/19china-takeaways-1/19china-takeaways-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image'