, 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Klepper, Jordan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wolf, Michelle', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'House of Cards (TV Program)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Jimmy Kimmel Live (TV Program)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Daily Show with Trevor Noah (TV Program)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-19T08:55:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Giovanni Russonello', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Giovanni', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Russonello', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/30ecb648-ca48-5a86-a1ab-eaf8de918212', 'word_count': 428, 'uri': 'nyt://article/30ecb648-ca48-5a86-a1ab-eaf8de918212'}, {'abstract': 'Katsudon — a bowl of rice topped with slices of pork cutlet, onions and barely cooked eggs — can be transcendent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/19/magazine/in-pursuit-of-cartoonish-perfection-in-a-japanese-rice-bowl.html', 'snippet': 'Katsudon — a bowl of rice topped with slices of pork cutlet, onions and barely cooked eggs — can be transcendent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like so much of the exuberant food imagery that I’m drawn to in anime, the katsudon in “Yuri!!! on Ice,” a series about a competitive figure skater in his early 20s, appeared as a less detailed but somehow more vivid version of itself. A Japanese rice bowl capped with golden slices of pork cutlet, held together with barely cooked eggs and translucent onions — textures exaggerated, colors saturated, aromas made visible — occasionally twinkling in soft focus, as if seen through a Vaseline-greased lens. “Is this what God eats?!” one character asked another, tre