oli moved about once a year. Most recently, Mr. Broccoli, a digital graphic designer, was renting a large one-bedroom in Peter Cooper Village for around $3,450 a month, and was eager to reduce his housing outlay.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Longtime Renter Gets a Lesson in Bidding', 'kicker': 'The Hunt', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When Buying Becomes an Option, It’s Time to Bid', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tudor City (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-19T09:00:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joyce Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joyce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/371ced4d-3951-55b8-9874-4378b1017dc2', 'word_count': 824, 'uri': 'nyt://article/371ced4d-3951-55b8-9874-4378b1017dc2'}, {'abstract': 'On Oct. 19, 1987, the stock market fell more than 20 percent. It would be comforting to believe a crash couldn’t recur. But we are still at risk.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/19/business/stock-market-crash-1987.html', 'snippet': 'On Oct. 19, 1987, the stock market fell more than 20 percent. It would be comforting to believe a crash couldn’t recur. But we are still at risk.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Oct. 19, 1987, was one of the worst days in stock market history. Thirty years later, it would be comforting to believe it couldn’t happen again.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'u