'value': 'Honda Motor Co Ltd', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mazda Motor Corp', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Toyota Motor Corp', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-19T11:30:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Soble', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Soble', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e34f3827-0c72-5043-943b-7c2ce5e5d538', 'word_count': 612, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e34f3827-0c72-5043-943b-7c2ce5e5d538'}, {'abstract': 'Sunday marks her last back-page interview for The Magazine’s “Talk” column. This time, she’s the one doing the introspection.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/19/reader-center/for-ana-marie-cox-goodbyes-can-be-awkward.html', 'snippet': 'Sunday marks her last back-page interview for The Magazine’s “Talk” column. This time, she’s the one doing the introspection.', 'lead_paragraph': 'All interviewers halfway decent at their jobs are genuinely curious about their subjects. Being the Talk columnist for the past two years meant that once a week, almost every week, I called a new person and tried to get to know them for an hour. We journalists often confuse soliciting new information with wanting to understand a subject. Chasing after a showy quote or treating the interview like an interrogation is a power trip, but it doesn’t mean you know your subject any better. My editors supported my decision to chase after introspection instead of scoops: Rather than wanting a truth that Talk subjects had been keeping from the world, I wanted one they’d also been keeping from themselves.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/21/reader-center/19-cox-combo/19-cox-combo-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 366, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/21/reader-center/19-cox-combo/19-cox-combo-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 366}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/21/reader-center/19-cox-combo/19-cox-combo-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 625, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/21/reader-center/19-cox-combo/19-cox-combo-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1186, 'width': 1943, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/21/reader-center/19-cox-combo/19-cox-combo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/21/reader-center/19-cox-combo/19-cox-combo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/21/reader-center/19-cox-combo/19-cox-combo-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Ana Marie Cox, Goodbyes Can Be Awkward', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At the Heart of a Celebrity Interview', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Magazines', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Celebrities', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-19T11:37:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'NewsDesk', 'section_name': 'Reader Center', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ana Marie Cox', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ana', 'middlename': 'Marie', 'lastname': 'Cox', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c3dd714-a9f6-5444-a9e2-f995b4472073', 'word_count': 887, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c3dd714-a9f6-5444-a9e2-f995b4472073'}, {'abstract': 'Pyotr Pavlensky was pictured on social media standing in front of flames at a Banque de France building on the Place de la Bastille.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/19/arts/pyotr-pavlensky-paris-fire.html', 'snippet': 'Pyotr Pavlensky was pictured on social media standing in front of flames at a Banque de France building on the Place de la Bastille.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Russian performance artist who was granted political asylum in France has been charged with property damage after apparently starting a fire at a French central bank building, the office of the Paris prosecutor said on Thursday.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/20/world/21Pavlensky/21Pavlensky-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/20/world/21Pavlensky/21Pavlensky-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/20/world/21Pavlensky/21Pavlensky-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': '