enting adults” sexual ethics? Not quite.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2017/10/19/the-age-of-consent-and-its-discontents/', 'snippet': 'Does Harvey Weinstein prove the case against a “consenting adults” sexual ethics? Not quite.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Amid the cascade of sexual assault stories coming out of liberal Hollywood\xa0in the wake of Harvey Weinstein’s fall, David French\xa0argues that the time is ripe for social conservatives to claim vindication in their critique of\xa0our society’s elevation of “consent” as the only rule of\xa0sexual morality:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Age of Consent and Its Discontents', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sexual Harassment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's Rights", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weinstein, Harvey', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-19T15:31:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e7fe0efd-4e6d-5b21-bc53-02fb287f0578', 'word_count': 1627, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e7fe0efd-4e6d-5b21-bc53-02fb287f0578'}, {'abstract': 'Engineers are finding ways to have cars do much more than take us from Point A to Point B — including producing and dispensing water.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/19/automobiles/wheels/car-water-engineers.html', 'snippet': 'Engineers are finding ways to have cars do much more than take us from Point A to Point B — including producing and dispensing water.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A few years ago, Doug Martin, an engineer at Ford, read an article about an unusual billboard in Lima, Peru: It was designed to collect and filter water that condenses on the billboard’s cool surfaces when humid air rolls in from the coast.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/20/business/20WHEELS1/20WHEELS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/20/business/20WHEELS1/20WHEELS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/20/business/20WHEELS1/20WHEELS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 416, 'width': 626, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/20/business/20WHEELS1/20WHEELS1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 416, 'width': 626, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/20/business/20WHEELS1/20WHEELS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/20/business/20WHEELS1/20WHEELS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/20/business/20WHEELS1/20WHEELS1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Would You Like My Car to Make You Some Water?', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When the Driver, Not the Car, Is Overheating', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martin, Doug (Engineer)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rollinger, John', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ford Motor Co', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-19T15:38:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'subsection_name': 'Wheels', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neal E. Boudette', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neal', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Boudette', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c46a06fc-738b-519f-9d50-bd3e66463cbf', 'word_count': 1063, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c46a06fc-738b-519f-9d50-bd3e66463cbf'}, {'abstract': 'In another fallout, a doctor who is accused of showing violent images to women as part of a study for the group has resigned from an Albany hospital.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/19/nyregion/complaints-by-ex-nxivm-members.html', 'snippet': 'In another fallout, a doctor who is accused of showing violent images to women as part of a study for the group has resigned from an Albany hospital.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Officials in New York State plan to review why regulators and others did not act after women involved with a secretive group reported they had been branded with a cauterizing device or traumatized during an “experiment,” said a spokesman for Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/20/nyregion/20CULT/20CULT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subT