com/2017/10/19/theater/review-peh-lo-tah-soccer-marc-bamuthi-joseph.html', 'snippet': 'Marc Bamuthi Joseph’s dance-theater show considers racism, colonialism and aging as refracted through the world’s most popular sport.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A line in the dance-theater show “/peh-LO-tah/” hits a timely raw nerve: “The Defender explains why Americans suck at soccer.” When these words flash on the back wall of the Brooklyn Academy of Music’s Harvey Theater, they are a biting reminder that the U.S. recently failed to qualify for the next World Cup, and in ignominious fashion at that.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/20/arts/20PEHLOTAH1/20PEHLOTAH1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/20/arts/20PEHLOTAH1/20PEHLOTAH1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/20/arts/20PEHLOTAH1/20PEHLOTAH1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/20/arts/20PEHLOTAH1/20PEHLOTAH1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/20/arts/20PEHLOTAH1/20PEHLOTAH1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/20/arts/20PEHLOTAH1/20PEHLOTAH1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/20/arts/20PEHLOTAH1/20PEHLOTAH1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: Life is Soccer, and Soccer is Life, in ‘/peh-LO-tah/’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'There’s Soccer, Then Everything Else', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': '/peh-LO-tah/ (Play)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Joseph, Marc Bamuthi', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garces, Michael John', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Academy of Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-19T16:13:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabeth Vincentelli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vincentelli', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa0e5b3b-c4a3-5735-8012-49cf80384d11', 'word_count': 497, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa0e5b3b-c4a3-5735-8012-49cf80384d11'}, {'abstract': 'This passionate historical drama from Robin Campillo follows young French activists through an emotional battle for respect and care.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/19/movies/bpm-beats-per-minute-review-aids-activism.html', 'snippet': 'This passionate historical drama from Robin Campillo follows young French activists through an emotional battle for respect and care.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is said of one of the characters in Robin Campillo’s “BPM (Beats Per Minute)” that “he lived his politics in the first person.” Even in translation and even in a movie set a quarter-century in the past, this suggestive phrase, which is part of a eulogy, cannot fail to resonate. The words, and the passionate, uncompromising sentiment behind them, offer an implicit rebuttal to the currently fashionable critique of “identity politics,” a phrase that seeks to trivialize struggles that are, for the people who practice such politics, a matter of life and death.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/20/arts/20bpm2/20bpm2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/20/arts/20bpm2/20bpm2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/20/arts/20bpm2/20bpm2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/20/arts/20bpm2/20bpm2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/20/arts/20bpm2/20bpm2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/20/arts/20bpm2/20bpm2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/20/arts/20bpm2/20bpm2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘BPM (Beats Per Minute)’ Captures the Fierce AIDS Fight', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Personal and Political Passions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Campillo, Robin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Valois, Arnaud (1984- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biscayart, Nahuel Perez', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'BPM (Beats Per Minute) (Movie)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-19T16:26:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/8053bb57-3cf7-5693-af19-a4e69ddbc48b', 'word_count': 753, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8053bb57-3cf7-5693-af19-a4e69ddbc48b'}, {'abstract': 'Cities in Syria and Iraq have been wrested from the Islamic State at a terrible cost. They are ghosts of their former glory.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/19/world/middleeast/islamic-state-reconstruction.html', 'snippet': 'Cities in Syria and Iraq have been wrested from the Islamic State at a terrible cost. They are ghosts of their former glory.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The declarations of victory played out across Iraq and Syria: The long campaigns to retake city after city from Islamic State militants had come to an end.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/19/world/20isis-kobani/20isis-kobani-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/19/world/20isis-kobani/20isis-kobani-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, '