e different answers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/20/books/review/the-meaning-of-belief-tim-crane-learning-religion.html', 'snippet': 'What is religion? New books by a philosopher, a sociologist and a theologian give different answers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The philosopher Tim Crane is an atheist. Though educated in a Catholic environment, he has come to believe that nothing exists beyond the world of everyday experience and scientific explanation — nothing transcendent. Some people look around and think, This can’t be all there is. Crane is not one of those people. That he avows atheism, as opposed to agnosticism, does not strike him as presumptuous or arrogant. He has considered the relevant evidence and arguments as best he can and drawn the most reasonable-seeming conclusion. What more is a thinker supposed to do? He is convinced religious believers are wrong.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/22/books/review/1022-BKS-IvoryTower/1022-BKS-IvoryTower-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 959, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/22/books/review/1022-BKS-IvoryTower/1022-BKS-IvoryTower-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 959}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/22/books/review/1022-BKS-IvoryTower/1022-BKS-IvoryTower-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 641, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/22/books/review/1022-BKS-IvoryTower/1022-BKS-IvoryTower-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1282, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credi