inal': 'By Karen Weintraub', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weintraub', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e49ea66-46df-55da-8d51-fd3140f52d2a', 'word_count': 463, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e49ea66-46df-55da-8d51-fd3140f52d2a'}, {'abstract': '“All my love,” our mother had written, but the paper wasn’t enough to contain it. So she wrapped it in a box.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/20/well/family/a-secret-goodbye-letter-from-my-mother.html', 'snippet': '“All my love,” our mother had written, but the paper wasn’t enough to contain it. So she wrapped it in a box.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the basement guest room, my dad and I pulled board games with most of the pieces missing from the corner of a closet and dumped them straight into the garbage. I thought of the nights my mother would pretend to send me to bed and, after my two younger sisters were tucked in and kissed good night, she’d signal for me to creep back down the dark hallway out to the living room. She and I would sit cross-legged on the floor, eating popcorn and playing Junior Monopoly — my bonus hour, just for big girls.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/18/well/family/well-family-letter/well-family-letter-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 507, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/18/well/family/well-family-letter/well-family-letter-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 507}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/18/well/family/well-family-letter/well-family-letter-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 865, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'su