riginal': 'By Michael Corkery', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Corkery', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0a30810-96a5-5b2e-8164-82a4c2540b98', 'word_count': 349, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0a30810-96a5-5b2e-8164-82a4c2540b98'}, {'abstract': 'The Yankees had always entered the World Series as regular-season champions. But, if they are Series bound this year, it will be on different terms.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/20/sports/yankees-wild-card-world-series.html', 'snippet': 'The Yankees had always entered the World Series as regular-season champions. But, if they are Series bound this year, it will be on different terms.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Yankees captured the 1927 World Series after losing just 44 games in the regular season, and they won only 87 before beating the Mets in the 2000 Series. But as they faced the Houston Astros in Game 6 of the American League Championship Series on Friday night, they were seeking a different sort of accomplishment: advancing to the World Series for the first time as a wild-card team.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/21/sports/21score1/21score1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/21/sports/21score1/21score1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/21/sports/21score1/21score1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'image