duled for pricing this week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/22/business/treasury-auctions-set-for-the-week-of-oct-23.html', 'snippet': 'The following tax-exempt fixed-income issues are scheduled for pricing this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Treasury’s schedule of financing this week includes Monday’s regular weekly auction of new three- and six-month bills and an auction of four-week bills on Tuesday.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Treasury Auctions Set for the Week of Oct. 23', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Treasury Auctions Scheduled To Be Held the Week of Oct. 23', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Municipal Bonds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Government Bonds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-23T01:16:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2680b3c-52ea-5f88-a318-33df76ae0467', 'word_count': 465, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2680b3c-52ea-5f88-a318-33df76ae0467'}, {'abstract': 'We learn more about a beloved “Star Trek” character in this week’s clunky episode.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/22/arts/television/star-trek-discovery-season-1-episode-6-recap.html', 'snippet': 'We learn more about a beloved “Star Trek” character in this week’s clunky episode.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With so many different casts, episodes, shows, movies and novels over the course of several decades, when it comes to “Star Trek,” there are bound to be violations of canon and plot holes that viewers just have to live with. Some are flagrant (The Enterprise being inexplicably kept from the Earth battle in “First Contact”) and others less so (Geordi La Forge saying Romulan ale is illegal in “Nemesis,” even though in “Deep Space Nine,” an admiral says this is no longer the case.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/22/arts/television/22trek-recap/22trek-recap-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 356, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/22/arts/television/22trek-recap/22trek-recap-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 356}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/22/arts/television/22trek-recap/22trek-recap-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 608, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/22/arts/television/22trek-recap/22trek-recap-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 712, 'width': 1200, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/22/arts/television/22trek-recap/22trek-recap-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/22/arts/television/22trek-recap/22trek-recap-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/22/arts/television/22trek-recap/22trek-recap-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Star Trek: Discovery’ Season 1, Episode 6: What’s Up With Sarek?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Star Trek: Discovery (TV Program)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS Corporation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rapp, Anthony', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-23T01:50:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sopan Deb', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sopan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Deb', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/52dcdfa1-ce63-5ab6-8c70-8625df102c2e', 'word_count': 887, 'uri': 'nyt://article/52dcdfa1-ce63-5ab6-8c70-8625df102c2e'}, {'abstract': 'Times Square is changing. But everyone still wants a cut.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/22/arts/television/the-deuce-recap-au-reservoir.html', 'snippet': 'Times Square is changing. But everyone still wants a cut.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The world of a David Simon show always comes first. For all the detail invested in the particulars of his characters’ lives and in the stories that animate them, Simon insists foremost on revealing how they fit into the larger ecosystem. In that respect, his approach is analogous to that of the great documentary filmmaker Frederick Wiseman, who has spent half a century trying to understand human behavior within the context of systems and institutions — like a high school (“High School”), a mental ward (“Titicut Follies”) or, more recently, the New York Public Library (“Ex Libris”). In a Simon show, individual actions can have far-reaching consequences, especially when the decisions of the powerful bear down on the vulnerable.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/20/watching/22deuce/22recaps-slide-SWFK-articleLarge.j