title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Amory', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/a3ca327b-1247-54f6-883c-faf3671363c0', 'word_count': 1064, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a3ca327b-1247-54f6-883c-faf3671363c0'}, {'abstract': 'The Communist leader held a lifelong contradiction in his attitudes toward revolution and state power.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/23/opinion/how-mao-molded-communism-to-create-a-new-china.html', 'snippet': 'The Communist leader held a lifelong contradiction in his attitudes toward revolution and state power.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Toward the end of his life, dying of Lou Gehrig’s disease, Mao Zedong claimed two achievements: leading the Communist revolution to victory and starting the Cultural Revolution. By pinpointing these episodes, he had underlined the lifelong contradiction in his attitudes toward revolution and state power.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/23/opinion/23macfarquharWeb/23macfarquharWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 523, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/23/opinion/23macfarquharWeb/23macfarquharWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 523}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/23/opinion/23macfarquharWeb/23macfarquharWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 892, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/23/opinion/23macfarquharWeb/23macfarquharWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1784, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'cro