ng from hairdos to baking to recreation, reflecting the fashions of those times: Trade Cards: An Illustrated History, Cornell University Library Division of Rare and Manuscript Collections, http://rmc.library.cornell.edu.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/25/dining/25burnercard/25burnercard-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 833, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/25/dining/25burnercard/25burnercard-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 833}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/25/dining/25burnercard/25burnercard-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 738, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/25/dining/25burnercard/25burnercard-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1350, 'width': 972, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/25/dining/25burnercard/25burnercard-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/25/dining/25burnercard/25burnercard-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/25/dining/25burnercard/25burnercard-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Online Exhibition of 19th Century Trade Cards', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Admire: 19th-Century Trade Cards Get an Online Platform', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cornell University', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kitchen Arts & Letters Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-23T19:58:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6257ad7a-6a5c-5951-9ef3-e16f8f4b90ca', 'word_count': 119, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6257ad7a-6a5c-5951-9ef3-e16f8f4b90ca'}, {'abstract': 'With sinking quarterly earnings and rising pressure on its stock, General Electric, the last surviving original member of the Dow, risks being pushed out.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/23/business/dealbook/the-dow-jones-without-ge-its-possible.html', 'snippet': 'With sinking quarterly earnings and rising pressure on its stock, General Electric, the last surviving original member of the Dow, risks being pushed out.', 'lead_paragraph': 'General Electric’s quarterly earnings, so bad that even the new chief executive, John Flannery, called them “horrible,” have put fresh pressure on a stock that’s down more than 25 percent this year. The performance threatens to add insult to injury. The last surviving original member of the Dow Jones industrial average risks being excluded from the benchmark.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Dow Jones Without G.E.? It’s Possible', 'kicker': 'Breakingviews', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Electric Company', 'rank': 1