st carry tadpoles to water. But the males aren’t choosy about whose tadpoles they transport.', 'lead_paragraph': 'South American poison frogs are known to most people for their poison — and their brilliant colors. But in almost all species, the poison frog carries tadpoles on its back to a rain forest pool for their final growth stage.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'One Simple Signal Sets Off a Complicated Frog Journey', 'kicker': 'ScienceTake', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Simple Signal Sets Off Complex Frog Journey', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frogs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Animal Behavior', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Harvard University', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Vienna', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guyana', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South America', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-24T07:30:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Gorman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gorman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d729698-8049-5b5d-be67-ca08546b4cca', 'word_count': 565, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d729698-8049-5b5d-be67-ca08546b4cca'}, {'abstract': 'Jill Freedman left behind a career in advertising to live at Resurrection City, an encampment on the National Mall that was part of the Poor Peoples Campaign. Her pictures show a different, human and optimistic side to a historical event that has been labeled a failure by some.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2017/10/24/finding-inspiration-in-the-struggle-at-resurrection-city/', 'snippet': 'Jill Freedman left behind a career in advertising to live at Resurrection City, an encampment on the National Mall that was part of the Poor Peoples Campaign. Her pictures show a different, human and optimistic side to a historical event that has ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Devastated by the assassination of the Rev. Dr. Martin Luther King Jr., Jill Freedman quit her copywriting job at a New York advertising agency and headed to Washington, D.C., to protest poverty and live among shacks and tents on the National Mall. Little more than an amateur photographer at the time, her commitment to racial and economic justice made her the only photographer who stayed and documented the entire six-week encampment known as Resurrection City.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Finding Inspiration in the Struggle at Resurrection City', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Resurrection City, 1968 (Book)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Mall (Washington, DC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Freedman, Jill (1939- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'King, Martin Luther Jr', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (DC)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-24T08:00:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maurice Berger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maurice', 'middlename'