fier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e032e5b-bc16-5c6e-b347-9bea47d0f641', 'word_count': 1564, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e032e5b-bc16-5c6e-b347-9bea47d0f641'}, {'abstract': 'The chef wants his Red Rooster restaurants in New York and London to be expressions of black culture, and he celebrates Harlem history in a new tour app.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/24/travel/chef-marcus-samuelsson-harlem-new-york-red-rooster.html', 'snippet': 'The chef wants his Red Rooster restaurants in New York and London to be expressions of black culture, and he celebrates Harlem history in a new tour app.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s understandable if it seems as though Marcus Samuelsson never sleeps. The affable New York-based chef and restaurateur, who recharged the Harlem dining scene with his restaurant Red Rooster in 2010, recently opened its first outpost, Red Rooster Shoreditch, along with the taqueria Tienda Roosteria, in London. He now operates a total of 15 restaurant brands, from Streetbird Rotisserie, also in Harlem, to Norda Bar & Grill in Göteborg, Sweden, where he grew up. Two restaurants are planned for downtown Newark and Greenpoint, Brooklyn.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/11/05/travel/05samuelsson-1/05samuelsson-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/11/05/travel/05samuelsson-1/05samuelsson-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/11/05/travel/05samuelsson-1/05samuelsson-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/11/05/travel/05samuelsson-1/05samuelsson-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/11/05/travel/05samuelsson-1/05samuelsson-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/11/05/travel/05samuelsson-1/05samuelsson-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/11/05/travel/05samuelsson-1/05samuelsson-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'From Cuisine to Apps, Marcus Samuelsson Is Dedicated to Diversity', 'kicker': 'Q&A', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Marcus Samuelsson on Touring Harlem.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Samuelsson, Marcus', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-24T09:00:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By John L. Dorman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Dorman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/41ef2403-c04a-523d-8bfa-086ee9a9935f', 'word_count': 806, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41ef2403-c04a-523d-8bfa-086ee9a9935f'}, {'abstract': 'The league had gone 532 days without a head coach being fired when the Suns ousted Earl Watson on Sunday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/24/sports/basketball/earl-watson-nba-coaches-fired.html', 'snippet': 'The league had gone 532 days without a head coach being fired when the Suns ousted Earl Watson on Sunday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the Phoenix Suns fired Earl Watson after three humbling losses to start the season, it brought an end to a remarkable stretch of stability in a famously volatile profession.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/24/sports/25steinpic1/25steinpic1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 412, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/24/sports/25steinpic1/25steinpic1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 412}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/24/sports/25steinpic1/25steinpic1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 703, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/24/sports/25steinpic1/25steinpic1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1406, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/24/sports/25steinpic1/25steinpic1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/24/sports/25steinpic1/25steinpic1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/24/sports/25steinpic1/25steinpic1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'N.B.A. Coaches Had Long Stretch of Stability. Has the Chopping Block Returned?', 'kicker': 'On Pro Basketball', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Firing Could Revive Coaching Carousel', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coaches and Managers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Phoenix Suns', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Watson, Earl (1979- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Assn', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-24T09:00:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marc Stein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marc', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4e3904e2-83c2-58a3-96a0-f7e95cf80745', 'word_count': 980, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4e3904e2-83c2-58a3-96a0-f7e95cf80745'}, {'abstract': 'Richard Matheson’s legacy is felt in stories of mysterious figures and horrible, dawning realities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/24/books/review/best-of-richard-matheson-new-horror-fiction.html', 'snippet': 'Richard Matheson’s legacy is felt in stories of mysterious figures and horrible, dawning realities.', 'lead_paragraph': '“When people talk about the genre, I guess they mention my name first,” Stephen King once wrote, “but without Richard Matheson, I wouldn’t be around.” The genre is, of course, horror. Victor LaValle, in his smart introduction to THE BEST OF RICHARD MATHESON (Penguin, paper, $17), states the case even more forcefully: “When you read modern horror, you are still reading Richard Matheson.” I’m not sure I can fully endorse that sentiment; with a lot of current horror fiction, I wish I were reading Matheson instead. But I know what LaValle means. When modern horror is good, Matheson (who died in 2013) is usually in there somewhere, a felt presence, like a ghost.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/29/books/review/1029-BKS-Rafferty-HORROR/1029-BKS-Rafferty-HORROR-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 418, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/29/books/review/1029-BKS-Rafferty-HORROR/1029-BKS-Rafferty-HORROR-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 418}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/29/books/review/1029-BKS-Rafferty-HORROR/1029-BKS-Rafferty-HORROR-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 714, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/29/books/review/1029-BKS-Rafferty-HORROR/1029-BKS-Rafferty-HORROR-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 979, 'width': 1404, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/29/books/review/1029-BKS-Rafferty-HORROR/1029-BKS-Rafferty-HORROR-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/29/books/review/1029-BKS-Rafferty-HORROR/1029-BKS-Rafferty-HORROR-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': No