nization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/e41ccc13-0444-50df-94c1-4351dedb8e6b', 'word_count': 1563, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e41ccc13-0444-50df-94c1-4351dedb8e6b'}, {'abstract': 'Opposition to the war in Vietnam was a great moral crusade, yet most Americans recall only enormous protests and social chaos.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/24/opinion/vietnam-antiwar-movement.html', 'snippet': 'Opposition to the war in Vietnam was a great moral crusade, yet most Americans recall only enormous protests and social chaos.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Vietnam antiwar movement, famous for its sound and fury, deserves credit for more. We were the first mass movement against a war in American history and one of its great moral crusades, yet most Americans recall only enormous protests and social chaos. In fact, the 10-year movement, in which I played a role, was a complex phenomenon that evolved strategically as circumstances changed. It can be broken down into four overlapping stages.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/24/opinion/24vietnamWeb/24vietnamWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 404, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/24/opinion/24vietnamWeb/24vietnamWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 404}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/24/opinion/24vietnamWeb/24vietnamWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 689, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/24/opinion/24vietnamWeb/24vietnamWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1378, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 's