-first-time-i-played-for-charles-mingus.html', 'snippet': 'He was a young, cocky jazz musician, making his way in the New York jazz world. And then, one night, the intimidating Charles Mingus walked into the club.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1977, a week after I graduated from New England Conservatory in Boston, I moved to New York to play with the greatest players in jazz — isn’t that why most young jazz musicians come to New York? Soon after I arrived, while I was picking up gigs at a variety of small jazz clubs in the Village (and one night at a piano bar on the Upper East Side, where I unhappily sang show tunes), I began going to Bradley’s, a bar on University Place owned by Bradley Cunningham, a gregarious, imposing former marine in his early 50s.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/29/arts/29HERSCH-COMBO/29HERSCH-COMBO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 272, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/29/arts/29HERSCH-COMBO/29HERSCH-COMBO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 272}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/29/arts/29HERSCH-COMBO/29HERSCH-COMBO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 464, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/29/arts/29HERSCH-COMBO/29HERSCH-COMBO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 928, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/29/arts/29HERSCH-COMBO/29HERSCH-COMBO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/29/arts/29HERSCH-COMBO/29HERSCH-COMBO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/29/arts/29HERSCH-COMBO/29HERSCH-COMBO-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Fred Hersch: The First Time I Played for Charles Mingus', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The First Time...I Played for Charles Mingus', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mingus, Charles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Good Things Happen Slowly: A Life in and Out of Jazz (Book)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-24T19:27:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Fred Hersch', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Fred', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hersch', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/187d92d5-2031-5fcb-b96b-030ce51ced50', 'word_count': 1039, 'uri': 'nyt://article/187d92d5-2031-5fcb-b96b-030ce51ced50'}, {'abstract': 'Anthony Atamanuik of “The President Show” never wanted a Trump victory, but it has been great for his career. Now he must avoid the many pitfalls of mocking the man.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/24/magazine/the-impossible-burden-of-playing-donald-trump.html', 'snippet': 'Anthony Atamanuik of “The President Show” never wanted a Trump victory, but it has been great for his career. Now he must avoid the many pitfalls of mocking the man.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Anthony Atamanuik has at least one thing in common with Donald Trump: Each man finds himself occupying a historic office, somewhat surprisingly and under high stakes. Trump’s office has been home to every president since Taft; Atamanuik’s used to belong to Stephen Colbert. I visited in late August, when Atamanuik was still settling in. There were big windows and high ceilings with exposed rafters. There was an executive bathroom. He showed me a “WristStrong” bracelet, a relic of Colbert’s injury, that he had fished out of the rafters using a decorative saber given to him by J.D. Amato, his friend and former co-executive producer. The saber had “truth” engraved on one side of the blade and “satire” on the other.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/24/magazine/24mag-anthony-ataminuik-6/24mag-anthony-ataminuik-6-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/24/magazine/24mag-anthony-ataminuik-6/24mag-anthony-ataminuik-6-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/24/magazine/24mag-anthony-ataminuik-6/24mag-anthony-ataminuik-6-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/24/magazine/24mag-anthony-ataminuik-6/24mag-anthony-ataminuik-6-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/24/magazine/24mag-anthony-ataminuik-6/24mag-anthony-ataminuik-6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thu