trend with economic and political ramifications.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/24/business/economy/future-jobs.html', 'snippet': 'A federal projection of the 2026 work force foresees greater polarization by wages, education and geography — a trend with economic and political ramifications.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A decade from now, the American economy could look much the way it does today — only more so. More dominated by the service sector amid the continued erosion of manufacturing jobs. More polarized in both earnings and geography. More tilted toward jobs that require at least a bachelor’s degree.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Peek at Future Jobs Shows Growing Economic Divides', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Experts Foresee a U.S. Work Force Defined by Ever Widening Divides', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bureau of Labor Statistics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-24T21:47:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Casselman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Casselman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd77ab05-bd02-5b51-8184-bd531492b2db', 'word_count': 830, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd77ab05-bd02-5b51-8184-bd531492b2db'}, {'abstract': 'Clayton Kershaw, the Dodgers’ ace, shut down the Astros with 11 strikeouts in seven innings.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/24/sports/dodgers-astros-world-series.html', 'snippet': 'Clayton Kershaw, the Dodgers’ ace, shut down the Astros with 11 strikeouts in seven innings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'World Series Game 1 was fairly easy to parse, as the Dodgers rode their dominant ace Clayton Kershaw to victory. Home runs by Chris Taylor and Justin Turner gave Kershaw more than enough cushion, and the Dodgers’ bullpen didn’t falter. But there were some key takeaways that could be important to watch as the series continues on Wednesday night. Here’s what we learned in Game 1:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/25/sports/25series-top/25series-top-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 439, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/25/sports/25series-top/25series-top-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 439}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/25/sports/25series-top/25series-top-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 749, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/25/sports/25series-top/25series-top-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1498, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/25/sports/25series-top/25series-top-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/25/sports/25series-top/25series-top-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/25/sports/25series-top/25series-top-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'th