tion': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c115dffe-c28d-5e85-a847-07f937a5ee8d', 'word_count': 167, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c115dffe-c28d-5e85-a847-07f937a5ee8d'}, {'abstract': 'The energy secretary’s plan to subsidize coal and nuclear power would upend efforts to promote fair competition in electricity markets.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/25/opinion/rick-perry-coal-antimarket.html', 'snippet': 'The energy secretary’s plan to subsidize coal and nuclear power would upend efforts to promote fair competition in electricity markets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lost in all the attention to the Trump administration’s effort to scuttle President Barack Obama’s clean power plan is its attempt to prop up the struggling coal industry by doing something very un-Republican — subsidizing it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/25/opinion/25freemanWeb/25freemanWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/25/opinion/25freemanWeb/25freemanWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/25/opinion/25freemanWeb/25freemanWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/25/opinion/25freemanWeb/25freemanWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/25/opinion/25freemanWeb/25freemanWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/25/opinion/25freemanWeb/25freemanWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/25/opinion/25freemanWeb/25freemanWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rick Perry’s Anti-Market Plan to Help Coal', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributors', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Solar Energy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wind Power', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Energy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coal', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Alternative and Renewable Energy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Energy Department', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Energy Regulatory Commission', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Rick', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-25T08:51:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jody Freeman and Joseph Goffman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jody', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Freeman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goffman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/13d085f6-ef80-5878-94f9-9b1e1a0c60c9', 'word_count': 1128, 'uri': 'nyt://article/13d085f6-ef80-5878-94f9-9b1e1a0c60c9'}, {'abstract': 'The magazine’s Ethicist columnist on exposing a deceased parent’s lie and reading a love letter to your mom from a former suitor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/25/magazine/should-i-reveal-that-my-dad-pretended-to-be-a-vietnam-vet.html', 'snippet': 'The magazine’s Ethicist columnist on exposing a deceased parent’s lie and reading a love letter to your mom from a former suitor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When he was alive, my father sometimes talked of his military service during the Vietnam War. He would oscillate between being open about details and not wanting to speak of his experience. Despite not having any “war buddies,” photographs or other tangible memorabilia, he offered enough details about his service (locations, activities and the name of a friend who was killed in front of him) that my siblings, as well as his friends, his wife and his wife’s family, believed he was a veteran. My mother and I, however, were never sure he was telling the truth about the nature of his service. For instance, when I was a teenager, I was with my father when he purchased a Purple Heart medal at an antiques fair. He explained that he had lost his, that it was possibly with his first wife. Although I thought it was odd he wouldn’t simply ask for it back, I was a young person who trusted her father, and I didn’t press him.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/29/magazine/29ethicist/29ethicist-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 896, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/29/magazine/29ethicist/29ethicist-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 896}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/29/magazine/29ethicist/29ethicist-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 686, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, 