cult-of-photography/', 'snippet': 'From its early days championing art photography to today’s shaping of personal identity on social media, Aperture has been leading the conversation on photography for 65 years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This year is the 65th anniversary of Aperture, which has shaped the conversation around photography through its magazine and books. Chris Boot, the executive director of the nonprofit Aperture Foundation spoke with James Estrin about the state of photography and its future. Their conversation has been edited for clarity and brevity.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Aperture at 65: Changing the ‘Cult’ of Photography', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chris Boot', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'White, Minor', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Magazines', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boot, Chris (1960- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'White, Minor', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'APERTURE FOUNDATION', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-26T08:00:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Estrin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Estrin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/17cfc7d3-7557-5096-9ff2-b7b1dc79848c', 'word_count': 2295, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17cfc7d3-7557-5096-9ff2-b7b1dc79848c'}, {'abstract': 'Jeff Flake spoke out. But where are the heroes with skin in the game?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/26/opinion/menace-trumpism-flake-republicans.html', 'snippet': 'Jeff Flake spoke out. But where are the heroes with skin in the game?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Senator Jeff Flake gave a powerful, even poetic speech on Tuesday rebuking Donald Trump and the menace of Trumpism consuming the damaged Republican Party. But he undercut the power of the speech by coupling it with the announcement of his impending retirement from the Senate.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/26/opinion/26blowWeb/26blowWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/26/opinion/26blowWeb/26blowWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/26/opinion/26blowWeb/26blowWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/26/opinion/26blowWeb/26blowWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/26/opinion/26blowWeb/26blowWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/26/opinion/26blowWeb/26blowWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/26/opinion/26blowWeb/26blowWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Menace of Trumpism', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Flake, Jeffrey L', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Corker, Robert Phillips Jr', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCain, John', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-26T08:51:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles M. Blow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/38fb540c-1a37-545d-b935-f459e5bf5d83', 'word_count': 884, 'uri': 'nyt://article/38fb540c-1a37-545d-b935-f459e5bf5d83'}, {'abstract': 'It’s tempting to believe the president is just trying to scare Kim Jong-un by acting crazy. If he is, it won’t work.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/26/opinion/the-madness-behind-trumps-madman-strategy.html', 'snippet': 'It’s tempting to believe the president is just trying to scare Kim Jong-un by acting crazy. If he is, it won’t work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'By now, it’s pretty obvious that President Trump sees foreign policy as an extension of the business world. In both, his strategy has been hard-nosed brinkmanship, trying to cow businessmen and world leaders like Kim Jong-un of North Korea with his refusal to compromise, even if getting his way risks significant damage to his interests and those of his friends.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/26/opinion/26stevensonWeb/26stevensonWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/26/opinion/26stevensonWeb/26stevensonWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/26/opinion/26stevensonWeb/26stevensonWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/26/opinion/26stevensonWeb/26stevensonWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/26/opinion/26stevensonWeb/26stevensonWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/26/opinion/26stevensonWeb/26stevensonWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/26/opinion/26stevensonWeb/26stevensonWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Madness Behind Trump’s ‘Madman’ Strategy', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nixon, Richard Milhous', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kennedy, John Fitzgerald', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Khrushchev, Nikita S', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-26T08:51:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Stevenson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stevenson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c4831f1-f192-52b5-8881-4977307faf6c', 'word_count': 902, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c4831f1-f192-52b5-8881-4977307faf6c'}, {'abstract': 'The most tragic aspect of Asia Argento’s being hounded in her own country is that the worst attacks weren’t coming from men.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/26/opinion/italian-feminism-asia-argento-weinstein.html', 'snippet': 'The most tragic aspect of Asia Argento’s being hounded in her own country is that the worst attacks weren’t coming from men.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MILAN — AMERICANS and Italians are such similar creatures: We both care about news only if it concerns us. That’s why in Italy there’s no such thing as the Harvey Weinstein scandal; here, it’s the Asia Argento scandal. Either way, it hasn’t made us look good.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/26/opinion/26sonciniWeb/26sonciniWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/26/opinion/26sonciniWeb/26sonciniWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/26/opinion/26sonciniWeb/26sonciniWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/26/opinion/26sonciniWeb/26sonciniWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/26/opinion/26sonciniWeb/26sonciniWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/26/opinion/26sonciniWeb/26sonciniWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/26/opinion/26sonciniWeb/26sonciniWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Failure of Italian Feminism', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Failure of Italian Feminism', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's Rights", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ARGENTO, ASIA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weinstein, Harvey', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-26T08:51:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Guia Soncini', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Guia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Soncini', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/5790f4c0-21b6-50f4-a9d3-0b84764ed1cb', 'word_count': 964, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5790f4c0-21b6-50f4-a9d3-0b84764ed1cb'}, {'abstract': 'John G. Roberts Jr. worries that people look at the Supreme Court justices and see partisans. His concern is a good thing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/26/opinion/politics-supreme-court-legitimacy.html', 'snippet': 'John G. Roberts Jr. worries that people look at the Supreme Court justices and see partisans. His concern is a good thing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s been a flood of hand-wringing and tut-tutting over some observations that Chief Justice John G. Roberts Jr. offered during the argument earlier this month in the big Wisconsin gerrymander case. He dismissed as “sociological gobbledygook” the metrics the plaintiffs offered for determining when districting decisions cross the line from ordinary politics to blunt force. He warned that the court would be putting its legitimacy in the eyes of the public on the line if it became the state-by-state arbiter of partisanship gone too far.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/26/opinion/26greenhosueWeb/26greenhosueWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/26/opinion/26greenhosueWeb/26greenhosueWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/26/opinion/26greenhosueWeb/26greenhosueWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/26/opinion/26greenhosueWeb/26greenhosueWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/26/opinion/26greenhosueWeb/26greenhosueWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/26/opinion/26greenhosueWeb/26greenhosueWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/26/opinion/26greenhosueWeb/26greenhosueWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Will Politics Tarnish the Supreme Court’s Legitimacy?', 'kicker': 'Contributing Op-Ed Writer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Redistricting and Reapportionment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roberts, John G Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McConnell, Mitch', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-26T08:51:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Linda Greenhouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Linda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greenhouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/76f83d55-81d5-5601-b5b4-b055ef3f0697', 'word_count': 1420, 'uri': 'nyt://article/76f83d55-81d5-5601-b5b4-b055ef3f0697'}, {'abstract': 'I’m glad to have a “rare genetic condition” instead of a “birth defect,” and a kinship with others like me.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/26/opinion/my-orphan-disease-has-given-me-a-new-family.html', 'snippet': 'I’m glad to have a “rare genetic condition” instead of a “birth defect,” and a kinship with others like me.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The members of my family share a number of traits, but not one of them looks quite like me.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/25/opinion/26disability/25disability-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/25/opinion/26disability/25disability-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/25/opinion/26disability/25disability-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/25/opinion/26disability/25disability-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/25/opinion/26disability/25disability-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/25/opinion/26disability/25disability-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/25/opinion/26disability/25disability-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'My ‘Orphan Disease’ Has Given Me a New Family', 'kicker': 'Disability', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'My ‘Orphan Disease’ Gave Me a New Family', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Genetics and Heredity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disabilities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-26T08:51:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rosemarie Garland-Thomson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rosemarie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Garland-Thomson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/8f13e477-5460-5e56-a5ea-2885f0b04430', 'word_count': 1312, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8f13e477-5460-5e56-a5ea-2885f0b04430'}, {'abstract': 'Democrats and Republicans need to act in the public interest and not for the powerful and connected.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/26/opinion/trump-made-the-swamp-worse-heres-how-to-drain-it.html', 'snippet': 'Democrats and Republicans need to act in the public interest and not for the powerful and connected.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Donald Trump’s pledges to “drain the swamp” of corruption in Washington attest to his genius for unintentional irony. Nepotism, egregious conflicts of interest, flights on the public dime to see Wimbledon and the eclipse — the Beltway wetlands are now wilder and murkier than ever.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/26/opinion/26telesWeb/26telesWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 355, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/26/opinio