 conditions. While treadmill and standing desks have grown in popularity, they provide a clear impact on our health but perhaps not on our work itself. We know that most people type better when they sit still than when they stand up or move about. But do they also think better?', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/29/magazine/29well/29mag-29well-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 591, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/29/magazine/29well/29mag-29well-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 591}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/29/magazine/29well/29mag-29well-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1009, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/29/magazine/29well/29mag-29well-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1500, 'width': 1523, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/29/magazine/29well/29mag-29well-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/29/magazine/29well/29mag-29well-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/29/magazine/29well/29mag-29well-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Thinking on Your Feet', 'kicker': 'Well ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Thinking on Your Feet', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Brain', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Exercise', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-26T09:00:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Well', 'subsection_name': 'Move', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gretchen Reynolds', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gretchen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reynolds', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a4a8cf0-70f0-55d5-a45c-c7cb7f5ea80a', 'word_count': 498, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a4a8cf0-70f0-55d5-a45c-c7cb7f5ea80a'}, {'abstract': 'I was too miserable to be polite, even to my hosts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/26/magazine/when-youre-the-bad-guest.html', 'snippet': 'I was too miserable to be polite, even to my hosts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A rich man asked me to dinner at his house. My wife and I had been fighting, and I didn’t want to go: to smile when I was hurt, to act reasonable and calm when I felt lost. But my wife wanted to go. Partly because she wanted to see the house but also partly because what is one to do? Stop one’s life?', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '46', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/29/magazine/29badguest-illo/29badguest-illo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/29/magazine/29badguest-illo/29badguest-illo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/29/magazine/29badguest-illo/29badguest-illo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 's