one, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Amie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tsang', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/784fc7cb-df15-5be5-b027-f8ddb24f4825', 'word_count': 1642, 'uri': 'nyt://article/784fc7cb-df15-5be5-b027-f8ddb24f4825'}, {'abstract': 'The maddening thing about slights is that they can be so slight, it’s hard to know.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/26/nyregion/it-wasnt-an-oversight-i-meant-to-ignore-you.html', 'snippet': 'The maddening thing about slights is that they can be so slight, it’s hard to know.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A friend went to an Off Broadway opening party earlier this month and had a feeling she had been slighted by an acquaintance but she is not sure. The acquaintance, who was one of the actors, responded to my friend’s congratulations with a cursory, “Yeah, thanks, I gotta get a drink” and moved on. On the other hand, there were a lot of people eager to talk to him; perhaps he did have only 20 seconds. This is the maddening thing about slights: they are often so slight it is difficult to know.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/29/nyregion/29MISINFORMED/29MISINFORMED-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 381, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/29/nyregion/29MISINFORMED/29MISINFORMED-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 381}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/29/nyregion/29MISINFORMED/29MISINFORMED-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 650, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit