: 696, 'uri': 'nyt://article/902cca05-a73b-5b91-87d1-4af120fe1da4'}, {'abstract': 'Musicians and fans in the city where he lived and worked were saddened by Fats Domino’s death, but determined to celebrate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/26/arts/music/fats-domino-new-orleans.html', 'snippet': 'Musicians and fans in the city where he lived and worked were saddened by Fats Domino’s death, but determined to celebrate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW ORLEANS — People woke up here this week to discover that Fats Domino, one of the last links to the moment when New Orleans R&B morphed into early rock ’n’ roll, was gone. From Mr. Domino’s Ninth Ward home to uptown, from the French Quarter to Metairie, musicians across the city pondered a future without Fats, while music fans reacted in the only appropriate way to mark a death in New Orleans: by having a party.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/28/arts/28domino-reax2/26domino-reax1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/28/arts/28domino-reax2/26domino-reax1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/28/arts/28domino-reax2/26domino-reax1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/28/arts/28domino-reax2/26domino-reax1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/28/arts/28domino-reax2/26domino-reax1-thumb