': "D'Aulaire's Book of Greek Myths (Book)", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-27T09:05:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/99361d4c-451a-5dfc-abae-10b500ecfa31', 'word_count': 24, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99361d4c-451a-5dfc-abae-10b500ecfa31'}, {'abstract': 'Bella Andre, who began her fiction career with a series about wilderness firefighters, had to evacuate her wine country house as the flames drew near.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/27/books/review/bella-andre-you-do-something-to-me-sullivans-best-seller-interview.html', 'snippet': 'Bella Andre, who began her fiction career with a series about wilderness firefighters, had to evacuate her wine country house as the flames drew near.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FIRE ON THE MOUNTAIN: The romance writer Bella Andre hit the combined fiction list last week with “You Do Something to Me,” the latest in a series of novels about the large and tight-knit Sullivan family. Andre — who began her fiction career with a trilogy about wilderness firefighters (“Never Too Hot,” etc.) — lives in Northern California’s wine country, where she frequently sets her books, and she told me in a recent email that the region’s devastating wildfires had come within a half mile of her property. “Our next-door neighbor came knocking on our door at 4 a.m. to let us know that the fire marshal had just called,” she said. “When we looked out our backyard windows, we could see flames all across the mountains that surround our house.” Andre woke her children and told them to pack a bag with anything they couldn’t replace. “Many stuffed animals ended up coming with us,” she said. “My husband and I threw some clothes in a bag, grabbed the dog, the kids’ baby pictures and financial papers that we don’t have digital copies of (note to self: take care of that immediately in case another natural disaster strikes!), and drove two hours south to my mother-in-law’s house.”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/11/05/books/review/1105-BKS-LIST/1105-BKS-LIST-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/11/05/books/review/1105-BKS-LIST/1105-BKS-LIST-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/11/05/books/review/1105-BKS-LIST/1105-BKS-LIST-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 773, 'width': 773, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/11/05/books/review/1105-BKS-LIST/1105-BKS-LIST-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 773, 'width': 773, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/11/05/books/review/1105-BKS-LIST/1105-BKS-LIST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/11/05/books/review/1105-BKS-LIST/1105-BKS-LIST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/11/05/books/review/1105-BKS-LIST/1105-BKS-LIST-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Romance Writer Who Almost Lost Her Home to California’s Wildfires', 'kicker': 'Inside the List', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None