d08d60d59'}, {'abstract': 'His rollicking piano style was the bridge to a new genre.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/27/opinion/jon-batiste-fats-domino.html', 'snippet': 'His rollicking piano style was the bridge to a new genre.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My first exposure to rock ’n’ roll came from watching mostly white bands like Nirvana, Korn and Limp Bizkit perform angsty songs on MTV. I bought some of their albums, but the genre didn’t really resonate with me until I learned that black people could be rock ’n’ roll artists too. None had as great an influence on me as Fats Domino, one of the biggest stars of the early rock ’n’ roll era, who died on Tuesday in Harvey, La.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jon Batiste: Fats Domino and the Rock ’n’ Roll I Didn’t Know', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pop and Rock Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Batiste, Jon (1986- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Domino, Fats', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Orleans (La)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-27T09:23:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Batiste', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Batiste', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/785ef14e-610a-5d10-bf95-a52ff742fdba', 'word_count': 842, 'uri': 'nyt://article/785ef14e-610a-5d10-bf95-a52ff742fdba'}, {'abstract': 'What do America’s teenagers have to say about American values?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/27/learning/teaching-with-what-doe