since it razed the Jungle, but migrants are still gathering and still suffering.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/27/opinion/migrants-calais-britain.html', 'snippet': 'France has made some improvements since it razed the Jungle, but migrants are still gathering and still suffering.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At least France recognizes that it has a problem. After Human Rights Watch charged in July that the police had used brutal tactics against immigrants in a camp near Calais, the government conducted an investigation and admitted this week that the abuses were “plausible.” The police were accused of spraying sleeping migrants, including children, with tear gas, using excessive force and confiscating blankets and sleeping bags from people forced to sleep in the open.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/28/world/28editorial-inyt/28editorial-inyt-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/28/world/28editorial-inyt/28editorial-inyt-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/28/world/28editorial-inyt/28editorial-inyt-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/28/world/28editorial-inyt/28editorial-inyt-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1361, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/28/world/28editorial-inyt/28editorial-inyt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnai