a3d75ffbffb4'}, {'abstract': 'A reboot in London and an upcoming futuristic staging in Paris ask whether and how opera companies can revamp the story of Puccini’s struggling young artists.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/27/arts/music/la-boheme-puccini-opera-metropolitan-london-paris.html', 'snippet': 'A reboot in London and an upcoming futuristic staging in Paris ask whether and how opera companies can revamp the story of Puccini’s struggling young artists.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — When Peter Gelb took over as general manager of the Metropolitan Opera a decade ago, he had a list of aging productions he considered replacing. Among them was Franco Zeffirelli’s proscenium-filling, crowd-delighting, hyper-realistic 1981 staging of Puccini’s “La Bohème,” about love and death among a gang of starving artists in 19th-century Paris.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/29/arts/29BOHEME8/29BOHEME8-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 382, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/29/arts/29BOHEME8/29BOHEME8-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 382}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/29/arts/29BOHEME8/29BOHEME8-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 652, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/29/arts/29BOHEME8/29BOHEME8-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1304, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/29/arts/29BOHEME8/29BOHEME8-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail',