ns on those long-term accounts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The lack of emergency savings can cause financial problems far beyond a short-term cash crunch, new research shows.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tapping Retirement Funds in Emergency May Cause Other Problems', 'kicker': 'Your Money Adviser', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tapping Retirement Funds in an Emergency May Cause Other Problems', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Retirement', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Savings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pensions and Retirement Plans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pew Charitable Trusts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': '401(k), 403(b) and 457 Plans', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-27T16:33:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/acedf255-83a6-5cf5-9158-29643a269158', 'word_count': 740, 'uri': 'nyt://article/acedf255-83a6-5cf5-9158-29643a269158'}, {'abstract': 'New York City plans to replace the MetroCard system with one that uses commuters’ phones or credit cards at turnstiles. Will passengers’ personal data be safe?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/27/nyregion/new-fare-system-metrocard-security-hacking.html', 'snippet': 'New York City plans to replace the MetroCard system with one that uses commuters’ phones or credit cards at turnstiles. Will passengers’ personal data be safe?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The MetroCard has had its downsides — “Please swipe again’’ are three words that are the curse of just about every New York City subway rider. More significantly, the wallet-size card has become outdated in a high-tech world. But at least it was hard to hack.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/28/nyregion/28subwayfarecard/00subwayfarecard-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/28/nyregion/28subwayfarecard/00subwayfarecard-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/28/nyregion/28subwayfarecard/00subwayfarecard-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/28/nyregion/28subwayfarecard/00subwayfarecard-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/28/nyregion/28subwayfarecard/00subwayfarecard-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/28/nyregion/28subwayfarecard/00subwayfarecard-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/28/nyregion/28subwayfarecard/00subwayfarecard-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New Fare System Raises Security Concerns, but Officials Promise Safety', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'MetroCard Replacement Will Be Safe, Officials Say', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subways', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Commerce and Payments', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transit Systems', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cyberattacks and Hackers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cubic Transportation Systems Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Transportation Authority', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-27T16:41:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Barron', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barron', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d1d5fff3-f603-5391-a65a-441b02e7c948', 'word_count': 1244, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d1d5fff3-f603-5391-a65a-441b02e7c948'}, {'abstract': 'It’s a big city, with plenty to do, see, hear and watch. Here’s a sampling of cultural highlights this weekend and over the week ahead.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/27/arts/10-things-to-do-in-nyc-now-morgan-library-master-drawings-halloween-festivals.html', 'snippet': 'It’s a big city, with plenty to do, see, hear and watch. Here’s a sampling of cultural highlights this weekend and over the week ahead.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This major group drawing show, running through Jan. 7, constitutes a grand summing-up of a career, of an art form and of an institution’s holdings. During the past 60 years, the New York art dealer Eugene V. Thaw and his wife, Clare Eddy Thaw, amassed a phenomenal drawing collection notable for its chronological breadth, running from the early Renaissance to the near present. This year they gave more than 400 items outright to the Morgan, expanding and deepening its range. The 150 works on view include a super-rare Andrea Mantegna, an unearthly Samuel Palmer and a soulful Vincent Van Gogh. HOLLAND COTTER', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/27/arts/27Listingsart/27Listingsart-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 564, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/27/arts/27Listingsart/27Listingsart-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 564}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/27/arts/27Listingsart/27Listingsart-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 963, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/27/arts/27Listingsart/27Listingsart-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1925, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/27/arts/27Listingsart/27Listingsart-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/27/arts/27Listingsart/27Listingsart-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/27/arts/27Listingsart/27Listingsart-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '10 Things to Do in NYC Now', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-27T16:44:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Webster', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Webster', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1feb6d2d-ea45-5c79-b93a-70d6f3d24e4c', 'word_count': 1171, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1feb6d2d-ea45-5c79-b93a-70d6f3d24e4c'}, {'abstract': 'In order to keep protections for one group of immigrants, kids fleeing violence might be turned away.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/27/opinion/sunday/dreamers-children-immigration-congress.html', 'snippet': 'In order to keep protections for one group of immigrants, kids fleeing violence might be turned away.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last August, Lesli Gonzalez, 22, got a phone call at 6 a.m. Did she know Doralinda Lopez de León, a Guatemalan girl who said she was running from danger and had been caught by Border Patrol agents entering the United States? Yes, Ms. Gonzalez said, she’s my cousin.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/29/opinion/sunday/29nazario/29nazario-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 402, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/29/opinion/sunday/29nazario/29nazario-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 402}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype