e_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/6687c95b-6f70-5e68-9305-467f58244708', 'word_count': 351, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6687c95b-6f70-5e68-9305-467f58244708'}, {'abstract': 'Why aren’t the potential 2020 contenders taking a stand on the way the country is heading?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/29/opinion/the-silence-of-the-democrats.html', 'snippet': 'Why aren’t the potential 2020 contenders taking a stand on the way the country is heading?', 'lead_paragraph': 'A recent speech by George W. Bush made headlines for its pointed criticisms of Donald Trump, but there was something else he said that I found far more compelling. As soon as he finished his thank-yous and his little jokes, Mr. Bush dived immediately into the heart of the crisis confronting Western democracies today:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/30/opinion/30tomasky/30tomasky-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 552, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/30/opinion/30tomasky/30tomasky-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 552}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/30/opinion/30tomasky/30tomasky-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 942, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/30/opinion/30tomasky/30tomasky-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1885, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/30/opinion/30tomasky/30tomasky-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/30/opinion/30tomasky/30tomasky-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/30/opinion/30tomasky/30tomasky-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Silence of the Democrats', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Silence of the Democrats', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, George W', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Democracy (Theory and Philosophy)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-30T01:28:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Tomasky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tomasky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/f42ae439-487b-57cd-88f1-d7e01a1ea412', 'word_count': 940, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f42ae439-487b-57cd-88f1-d7e01a1ea412'}, {'abstract': 'The finale was a violent reminder of the price women pay for misogyny.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/29/arts/television/the-deuce-recap-season-1-finale-my-name-is-ruby.html', 'snippet': 'The finale was a violent reminder of the price women pay for misogyny.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first season of “The Deuce” ends, fittingly, with a screening of “Deep Throat,” the 1972 box office phenomenon that ushered in the era of “porno chic,” when hard-core pornography infiltrated theaters and production values rose accordingly. There’s gold in them hills for the gangsters and pornographers that populate Times Square, and perhaps some measure of celebrity, too, given the star treatment Linda Lovelace receives as she ascends to the V.I.P. section. Yet creators David Simon and George Pelecanos, who wrote the episode, surely know the behind-the-scenes story of “Deep Throat” and how it epitomizes the exploitation and abuse at the heart of the industry. The particulars are not easily sorted out, but Lovelace, under her real name, Linda Boreman, later claimed her husband coerced her into sex work, telling the Meese Commission, “Virtually every time someone watches that movie, they’re watching me being raped.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/26/watching/29deuce/29recaps-slide-ZJQR-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/26/watching/29deuce/29recaps-slide-ZJQR-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/26/watching/29deuce/29recaps-slide-ZJQR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/26/watching/29deuce/29recaps-slide-ZJQR-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/26/watching/29deuce/29recaps-slide-ZJQR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/26/watching/29deuce/29recaps-slide-ZJQR-thumbStandard.jpg',