tps://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/30/education/edlife/christine-eustrade-french-lesson.html', 'snippet': 'A textbook featuring a stylish student with the world on a string charmed a 12-year-old, and changed her life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like most people, I started studying a second language at the exact worst time in life. Junior high falls just after the period when one might pick up a language easily and right before most people are able to grasp what a valuable skill it is, making it a cruelly perfect sweet spot for frustration. As if dealing with unfamiliar grammar isn’t challenging enough, existentialist works like “Huis Clos” and “L’Etranger” are introduced not long after, in high school — a true philosophy of the absurd.', 'print_section': 'ED', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/11/05/education/05ed-notebook2/05ed-notebook2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/11/05/education/05ed-notebook2/05ed-notebook2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/11/05/education/05ed-notebook2/05ed-notebook2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/11/05/education/05ed-notebook2/05ed-notebook2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/11/05/education/05ed-notebook2/05ed-notebook2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumb