abstract': 'This chicken confit from D’Artagnan is a versatile ingredient for tacos, stir-fries and more.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/30/dining/chicken-confit.html', 'snippet': 'This chicken confit from D’Artagnan is a versatile ingredient for tacos, stir-fries and more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'All confit is not duck, and D’Artagnan has introduced a chicken version made from the legs and thighs of Green Circle Chickens — the tasty free-range birds raised on chef’s vegetable scraps. The confit, slowly cooked in duck fat, is rich, moist, easily boned, leaner than the duck version and astonishingly versatile. Chicken salad? A quick stir-fry with mushrooms? With pasta? In tacos or enchiladas? For potpies? Ramen bowls? Skillet suppers? Keep it on hand in the fridge or freezer: Chicken confit, two legs and thighs, $9.99, dartagnan.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/11/01/dining/01BURNERCONFIT/01BURNERCONFIT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 470, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/11/01/dining/01BURNERCONFIT/01BURNERCONFIT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 470}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/11/01/dining/01BURNERCONFIT/01BURNERCONFIT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 802, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/11/01/dining/01BURNERCONFIT/01BURNERCONFIT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1604, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/11/01/dining/01BURNERCONFIT/01BURNERCONFIT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/11/01/dining/01BURNERCONFIT/01BURNERCONFIT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/11/01/dining/01BURNERCONFIT/01BURNERCONFIT-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Chicken Confit for Weeknight Experimentation', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Cook: Switching Things Up With Chicken Confit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chickens', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "D'Artagnan", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-30T20:14:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7fb8fe23-df3d-5ef0-8a0f-2cffb9e7dc21', 'word_count': 111, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7fb8fe23-df3d-5ef0-8a0f-2cffb9e7dc21'}, {'abstract': 'Massimo Bottura will discuss the future of food at the 92nd Street Y.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/30/dining/massimo-bottura-food-waste-talk.html', 'snippet': 'Massimo Bottura will discuss the future of food at the 92nd Street Y.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The real passion for the chef Massimo Bottura — whose Osteria Francescana restaurant in Modena, Italy, is often ranked among the best in the world — is a campaign to reduce food waste and feed the underprivileged. Mr. Bottura will discuss these socially conscious efforts with Fabio Parasecoli, a professor at the New School; Danny Bowien, the chef and owner of Mission Chinese Food; Daniel Humm, of Eleven Madison Park; and Kathryn Garcia, the New York City’s commissioner of the Department of Sanitation. Mitchell Davis of the James Beard Foundation will moderate: “Massimo Bottura and Friends on the Future of Food: Can Chefs Save the Planet?” 8 p.m., Nov. 9, $35, 92nd Street Y, 1395 Lexington Avenue (92nd Street), 92y.org, 212-415-5500.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/11/01/dining/01burnertalkA/01burnertalkA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/11/01/dining/01burnertalkA/01burnertalkA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/11/01/dining/01burnertalkA/01burnertalkA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/11/01/dining/01burnertalkA/01burnertalkA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/11/01/dining/01burnertalkA/01burnertalkA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/11/01/dining/01burnertalkA/01burnertalkA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/11/01/dini