sions to Judaism in Israel, the backlash was swift and fierce.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/31/world/31israel1/31israel1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/31/world/31israel1/31israel1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/31/world/31israel1/31israel1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/31/world/31israel1/31israel1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/31/world/31israel1/31israel1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/31/world/31israel1/31israel1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/31/world/31israel1/31israel1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Jews of the Diaspora Bring Their Cause to the Israeli Public', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jews of Diaspora Highlight Their Cause', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Western Wall (Jerusalem)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jerusalem (Israel)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Netanyahu, Benjamin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-30T21:44:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By David M. Halbfinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a3f11f55-2859-5cd1-915e-7a1cba6af22d', 'word_count': 1086, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a3f11f55-2859-5cd1-915e-7a1cba6af22d'}, {'abstract': 'Diners will be able to add a meaty chili in the Texas style to hot dogs, cheeseburgers and fries.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/30/dining/shake-shack-chili.html', 'snippet': 'Diners will be able to add a meaty chili in the Texas style to hot dogs, cheeseburgers and fries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Shake Shacks have added chili. “It’s such an American thing, so it suits us,” said Mark Rosati, the chain’s culinary director. Texas-style meat chili (no beans) comes on a chili cheese dog, a chili cheeseburger and chili cheese fries, all finished with chopped scallions. The robust topping adds moderate heat primarily from ancho chiles and chiles de arbol, roasted, smoked and ground in-house. A cup of the chili is not on the menu, but it is available on request: Chili specialties, $4.89 to $9.69, starting Monday for orders placed through the Shake Shack app in restaurants in the United States (except in sports arenas and airports) starting Thursday, shakeshack.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/11/01/dining/01BURNERCONFIT-1509139258575/01BURNERCONFIT-1509139258575-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 673, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop