7-year-old man was arrested after a woman disappeared, and the Japanese news media said parts of nine bodies had been found in his house near Tokyo.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOKYO — A police search for a missing Tokyo woman who had sought a suicide partner led them to a townhouse with nine mutilated bodies and coolers containing heads covered in cat litter, Japanese media reported Tuesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/11/01/world/01japan-1/01japan-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 435, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/11/01/world/01japan-1/01japan-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 435}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/11/01/world/01japan-1/01japan-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 743, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/11/01/world/01japan-1/01japan-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1485, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/11/01/world/01japan-1/01japan-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/11/01/world/01japan-1/01japan-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/11/01/world/01japan-1/01japan-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Police Find Severed Heads in Coolers in Serial Killer Case That Stuns Japan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nine Bodies Discovered By the Police In Japan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Serial Murders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shiraishi, Takahiro', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders, Attempted Murders and Homicides', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kanagawa Prefecture (Japan)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-31T07:55:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hisako Ueno and Austin Ramzy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hisako', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ueno', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Austin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ramzy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d1d7f443-4a6a-54b0-aa60-16950f4e29e6', 'word_count': 428, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d1d7f443-4a6a-54b0-aa60-16950f4e29e6'}, {'abstract': 'Lam Duc-Hien, a Vietnamese photographer, first imagined Iraq to be full of tanks and violence. But after documenting the Kurdish region of Iraq for more than two decades, he found something very different.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2017/10/31/kurdish-independence-referendum-lam-duc-hien/', 'snippet': 'Lam Duc-Hien, a Vietnamese photographer, first imagined Iraq to be full of tanks and violence. But after documenting the Kurdish region of Iraq for more than two decades, he found something very different.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A serpentine river gently cuts through a mountain plateau. Shepherds tend their flock while young men hunt wild game, fish along ancient tributaries or kayak over rapids. This pleated landscape of rolling hills and jagged mountains is most verdant in spring, when the junipers are full, the grass a vibrant emerald. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Untold Quiet of Kurdish Iraq', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kurds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Erbil (Iraq)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-31T08:00:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kenneth R. Rosen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kenneth', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Rosen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a25cf84-8a0b-5e9e-aca8-31ee5942f256', 'word_count': 720, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a25cf84-8a0b-5e9e-aca8-31ee5942f256'}, {'abstract': 'Denouncing judges who rule against the president is an attack on the independence and integrity of the entire judiciary.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/31/opinion/myth-judicial-resistance-integrity.html', 'snippet': 'Denouncing judges who rule against the president is an attack on the independence and integrity of the entire judiciary.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Imagine this: In the days after a new president’s central domestic policy initiative becomes law, a number of state attorneys general and public interest groups — committed ideological opponents of the president — march into the courts seeking its invalidation. By cherry-picking friendly district judges in parts of the country hostile to the president’s politics and values, in judicial circuits with longstanding reputations for legal approaches more sympathetic to one end of the political spectrum, these challengers become remarkably successful in persuading at least some of the courts to embrace legal theories soundly criticized by many in the legal academy — and novel even in the views of some of their proponents. And when these lawsuits finally reach the Supreme Court, the justices deliver a mixed verdict, upholding the core of the president’s initiative, but also sustaining enough of the challengers’ objections that all involved can claim some kind of victory.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/31/opinion/31lithwickWeb/31lithwickWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 409, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/31/opinion/31lithwickWeb/31lithwickWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 409}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/31/opinion/31lithwickWeb/31lithwickWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 698, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/31/opinion/31lithwickWeb/31lithwickWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1396, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/31/opinion/31lithwickWeb/31lithwickWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/31/opinion/31lithwickWeb/31lithwickWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/31/opinion/31lithwickWeb/31lithwickWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Dangerous Myth of the Judicial ‘Resistance’', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributors', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-10-31T08:51:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dahlia Lithwick and Stephen I. Vladeck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dahlia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lithwick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': 'I.', 'lastname': 'Vladeck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/e470bfec-a989-557c-9187-6c844fade128', 'word_count': 1097, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e470bfec-a989-557c-9187-6c844fade128'}, {'abstract': 'I noticed that boys in my classes always seem more confident. That’s why my Girl Scout troop created a new patch.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/31/opinion/im-10-and-i-want-girls-to-raise-their-hands.html', 'snippet': 'I noticed that boys in my classes always seem more confident. That’s why my Girl Scout troop created a new patch.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last year on a fourth-grade field trip, I noticed that all the boys stood in the front and raised their hands while most of the girls politely stayed in the back and were quiet. It made me upset.',