one else’s project.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2016, after Andrew Stanton finished his billion-dollar-grossing movie “Finding Dory,” for which he was a co-writer and co-director, he thought about what he wanted to do next. “I was looking to take a long-term break from animation,” he said in a phone interview from his offices in San Francisco. It takes four years to make a Pixar film, he said, “and those years get shorter as I get older.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/11/01/arts/01stranger-qa-sub/01stranger-qa-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 279, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/11/01/arts/01stranger-qa-sub/01stranger-qa-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 279}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/11/01/arts/01stranger-qa-sub/01stranger-qa-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 476, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/11/01/arts/01stranger-qa-sub/01stranger-qa-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 952, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/11/01/arts/01stranger-qa-sub/01stranger-qa-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/11/01/arts/01stranger-qa-sub/01stranger-qa-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/11/01/arts/01stranger-qa-sub/01stranger-qa-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height